1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Erik Gustavsson (Ängaätt)=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Son of Gustav Laurensson (Ängaätt) and Margareta Olofsdotter (Hjulstaätt)
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://www.adelsvapen.com/genealogi/Svarte_Sk%C3%A5ning Adelsvapen Geneologies Svarte Skåning]
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT '''TABLE 5'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Answered Åke Jönsson .''' Said to be 60 years old in 1477, although he is mentioned in letters after his brother Ture, who was described as 50 years old in 1477. Probably identical to the "Swarte Akow" which in 1438 together wi
2 CONC th Swedes was enrolled at the University of Leipzig. Appears in Sweden at the earliest in 1440. Was knighted between 1446 and 19.1 1449, so apparently at King Karl's coronation in Uppsala 29.6 1448. Was a councilor at least from 1
2 CONC 450 and is mentioned as a nobleman at Ringstadaholm 19.1 1451 and 1453. In 1454 he received a deed of grant of Brandaborg, which supposed to be identical to Karlsholm, where he was a courtier in 1457. From between 1457 and 1459 he
2 CONC  was a courtier in Nyköping. Became district chief in Rönö hd in Södermanland between 1455 and 26.1 1458, which he was still 3.6 1462, and lawman in Södermanland 1457 or 1458, which he was still 23.11 1494. Died between 23.11 1494
2 CONC  and 15.8 1495 and was buried in Krokek's monastery. '''Gave 18.1 1445 morning gift to Mechtild Clausdotter, who was still alive 4.5 1460 and was the daughter of Claus Plata in marriage with Cecilia Nilsdotter, whose family's coat
2 CONC  of arms carried the split shield with the left field checkered. On 24 October 1468, Svarte Åke Jönsson gave a morning gift to Birgitta Gregersdotter, who was the daughter of the Riksdag Gregers Matsson ( Lillie ) in marriage to A
2 CONC nna Johansdotter ( Pike ) and died between 1 November 1503 and 12 March 1504 and was buried in Krokek's monastery.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Children:'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * 1. '''Ingeborg Åkedotter.''' Died between 6.2 1477 and 1.2 1480. Received 17.1 '''1463 gift of morning from the knight and councilor Staffan Bengtsson (Vinstorpaätten), who in 1459 became the widower of Birgitta Olofsdotter (Has
2 CONC ) at the latest and fell in the battle of Brunkeberg 10.10 1471. Was 6.2 1477 remarried with the councilor Erik Gustavsson ( Ängaätten ) who died between 12.9 1480 and 7.5 1482.'''
2 CONT * 1. '''Svarte Jöns Åkeson.''' Supposed to be the "Jhoannes Swarte de Svecia" who in 1467 was promoted to baccalaureus in canon law at the University of Leipzig and then received at the University of Greifswald and in Sept. 1476 w
2 CONC as enrolled at the University of Rostock. Was promoted before 12.2 1479 from canon to archdeacon in Strängnäs. Probably the "Iohannes Swartz de Stregeness" who in 1483 was enrolled at the University of Leipzig. Died as archdeacon 
2 CONC in Strängnäs in 1502. Arfrid Åkedotter. Died no later than 1490 and had then been married to the Riksrader Jöns Knutsson ( Tre rosor ), who in 1477 was the widower of Ingegerd Eriksdotter (Skanke), after Arfrid's death remarried E
2 CONC rmegard Fickedotter ( Bülow ), and died between 1496 and 1498.
2 CONT * 2. '''Mechtild (Brask)''', p. 138). Probably died young.
2 CONT * 2. '''Örjan Åkeson.''' Died young.
2 CONT * 2. '''Axel Åkeson.''' Appears at the earliest on 2.2 1489, died in 1497 or 1498 and was buried in Krokek's monastery.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ==SDHK no: [https://sok.riksarkivet.se/?ValdSortering=DatumStigande&PageSize=50&Sokord=ekebyborna&EndastDigitaliserat=False&AvanceradSok=False&page=29&FacettState=uw8klQ%3Ao&postid=sdhk_30674&tab=post 30674]
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Dating:, 1480 February 2, Place of issue: Åkerö'''
2 CONT
2 CONT The knight Svarte Åke Jönsson in Åkerö makes an agreement on behalf of his granddaughter Mektild Staffansdotter with his 'brother-in-law' (= son-in-law) Erik Gustavsson about silver, gold and chattels in Kavlås and in Vadstena whi
2 CONC ch are Mektild's after his late father Staffan (Bengtsson). Erik is to keep Vallby in Lunda parish, *Näs in Ekebyborna parish as well as Snösbäck and a farm in Agnestad in Agne(stads) parish.
2 CONT
2 CONT Literature and commentary, See DMS, Södermanland 2:3, p. 114. About Mektild Staffansdotter (Vinstorpaätten) see ÄSF I, p. 105. On Erik Gustavsson (Ängaätten) see ÄSF II, p. 118. Cf. SDHK no. 29420 and SDHK no. 30673 
