2 CONT
2 CONT SDHK-nr: [https://sok.riksarkivet.se/?Sokord=greta&EndastDigitaliserat=false&AvanceradSok=False&page=16&postid=sdhk_13306&tab=post#tab 13306]
2 CONT
2 CONT Utfärdat: 13870623, Stockholm
2 CONT Innehåll: Kung Albrekt av Sverige etc. kungör att han på Greta Dumes, Bo Jonssons änkas, och hennes barns vägnar givit Jakob (=Jeppe) Djäken i uppdrag att tills vidare förvalta Åbofögderiet för Greta Dume. En del av inkomsten dära
2 CONC v anslogs till avbetalningen av den fordran på 8000 mark penningar eller 20.000 mark svenska penningar som Jakob Djäken hade på Bo Jonssons arvingar.
2 CONT
2 CONT Greta Dumes 4 bröder och riddaren Henrik van Brandis beseglar.
2 CONT
2 CONT ''Källor''
2 CONT
2 CONT Original: or. perg. Mecklenburgisches Landeshauptarchiv, Schwerins
2 CONT
2 CONT SDHK-nr: [https://sok.riksarkivet.se/?Sokord=greta&EndastDigitaliserat=false&AvanceradSok=False&page=17&postid=sdhk_13628&tab=post#tab 13628]
2 CONT
2 CONT Utfärdat: 13891227, Stockholm Innehåll: Otto Beyenvlet, hövitsman på Stockholms hus, riddarna Johan van Sköneberg, Markvard Görtz och Johan Dume utfärdar lejdebrev för hustru Greta Dume, änka efter Bo Jonsson, hennes son Knut Boss
2 CONC on och hennes följe, som berättigar till inresa i och utresa ur Stockholm ända till ”fastogangs sunodagh” följande år, ohindrad ”fore oss oc fore allom them son gøra oc lata wilia fore warss kæra Herra, konung Albrictz skuld”.
2 CONT
2 CONT Utfärdarna beseglar.
2 CONT
2 CONT ---------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT ==English==
2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Margareta_Dume
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Margareta (Greta) Lambrektsdotter Dume'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Often referred to as '''Greta Dume''', (d. 1410), was a Swedish heiress. She played a political role in the struggle between Albert, King of Sweden and Queen Margaret I of Denmark over the Swedish throne in the late 14th century.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Margareta Dume''' belonged to an originally German noble family who lived in Swedish Finland since 1362. In 1373, she married the powerful Bo Jonsson (Grip), and he gave important posts to her brothers. In 1386, she became a wi
2 CONC dow. In the will of her late spouse, she had been denied the larger part of his wast fortune and any influence upon his affairs. She contested this, left for the Swedish royal court and made the King the protector of her and her c
2 CONC hildren's rights in the civil war-like conflict which erupted over the inheritance of her spouse in 1387. She also declared her support of King Albert as his ally and loyalist in his struggle against queen Margaret. This made it p
2 CONC ossible for her to use the king's supporters in the great inheritance feud. It is noted that she had an important political position, as she exerted influence upon certain affairs of state due to her important support to the king:
2 CONC  in 1388, for example, the king granted a member of the nobility the return of his confiscated property upon her request. She was present at the Swedish court in 1389, the same year Albert was deposed, but left for Germany after t
2 CONC his. In 1394, she married the Swedish noble Bengt Niklisson, returned to Sweden with him and made her peace with queen Margaret.
2 CONT
2 CONT -----
