1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == Magnus Gislason (Sparre av Aspnäs)==
2 CONT
2 CONT * Son of Gisle Elinason (Sparre av Aspnäs) and Margareta Bengtsdotter ( Bossons ätt ) 
2 CONT
2 CONT [http://www.adelsvapen.com/genealogi/Sparre_av_Aspn%C3%A4s#TAB_5 '''Magnus Gislason'''] (son of Gisle Elinason, Appears at the earliest in 1335. Became a knight for some of the years 1335—1341. Mentioned as the National Council fr
2 CONC om 1362 but seems to have been excluded from the Council in 1371. Appears as district governor in Tjust 1361—1369 and in Gästrikland 1370. Lived 1352 and 1353 apparently at Örby (now Örbyhus) in Vendels sn, Örbyhus hd in Uppland, 
2 CONC but bought 18.1.1357 from his brother Barnam Gislason stone house at Aspnäs in Östervåla sn. Våla hd in Uppland and dated several letters on Aspnäs from 1362 to 1370, which is why it must then have been his seat. Died in 1372 or 1
2 CONC 373. '''Married at the latest in 1346 with Birgitta Knutsdotter,''' which was still alive in 1373, but died in 1381, was the daughter of the knight and councilor Knut Folkason ( Algot Sons lineage ) and Margaret Tyrgilsdotter ( Ty
2 CONC rgils Knutsson's lineage) and previously married Erik Boberg, who was still living in 1335.
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Ingeborg Magnusdotter,''' Was probably still alive in 1373 but was dead in 1375, when her husband mentioned below was married. Married at the latest in 1369 with the knight and the national council Bengt Filipsson ( Ulv ), wh
2 CONC o was previously married to Birgitta Karlsdotter (shared shield; daughter of Karl Näskonungsson), who was still alive in 1359, and earlier in 1375 married Cecilia Ulfsdotter ( Ulvåsaätt ) and died around 1382. Their descendants in
2 CONC herited Magnus Gislason's Aspnäs farm.
2 CONT * '''Helena Magnusdotter,''' Probably died at the earliest in 1373 but not later than 1380. Married by 1369 to the knight, the Council of Ministers and the Finnish lawman Arvid Gustafsson ( Sparre av Vik ), who died in 1379 or 138
2 CONC 0. Their descendants inherited Magnus Gislason's former farm Örby.
2 CONT
2 CONT == Swedish Diplomatarium's National Archives of Medieval Letters
2 CONT
2 CONT == SDHK No: [https://sok.riksarkivet.se/?Sokord=Magnus+Gislesson&EndastDigitaliserat=false&Fritext=Magnus+Gislesson&AvanceradSok=True&page=17&postid=sdhk_7920&tab=post&FacettState=undefined%3Ac%7C#tab 7920]
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Dating: 1361 March 4, of Issue: Rönö'''
2 CONT
2 CONT The knight Magnus Gislesson and his wife Birgitta Knutsdotter exchange their goods in Älgenäs in the Lofta parish, Svinhult in the same parish, Sörby in the Landeryds parish and, with certain conditions, Åsmestad in Slaka parish t
2 CONC o St. Erik's chapel in Linköping and its holder Mr Nils against 12 barrels of barley and 3 land money in annual debts in Utnäs in the Säby parish in Västmanland.  The issuers seal. - https://sok.riksarkivet.se/dokument/sdhk/7920.p
2 CONC df
2 CONT
2 CONT == SDHK No: [https://sok.riksarkivet.se/?Sokord=Magnus+Gislesson&EndastDigitaliserat=false&Fritext=Magnus+Gislesson&AvanceradSok=True&page=18&postid=sdhk_10416&tab=post&FacettState=undefined%3Ac%7C#tab 10416]
2 CONT
2 CONT * Dating: 1373 October 11, of Issue: Uppsala
2 CONT
2 CONT Birgitta Knutsdotter, widow of well-knighted knight Magnus Gislesson, and (her grandsons) knights Bengt Filipsson and Arvid Gustafsson, all heirs to said Magnus , donate to Uppsala Cathedral's building fund 21 1/2 öesland land in 
2 CONC the village of Hässleby in Börje parish. As a condition of the gift, it is stated that for Mr. Magnus in the cathedral a yearly meeting with Mass and singing vigils will be celebrated the day after the celebration of the Holy Cros
2 CONC s's reunion (4/5).  The issuers seal. - https://lbiiif.riksarkivet.se/sdhk!10416_10416.jpg/full/1000,666/0/default.jpg
2 CONT
2 CONT == SDHK No: [https://sok.riksarkivet.se/?Sokord=Magnus+Gislason+&EndastDigitaliserat=false&AvanceradSok=False&page=1&postid=sdhk_5281&tab=post&FacettState=undefined%3Ac%7C#tab 5281]
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Dating: 1346 March 8'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''The knight Magnus Gislason''' exchanges for the abbess in Riseberga monastery 6 herb land in Boskulla and 8 herb land in Dværstad, and orders Lidinvard Holmgersson to put her in legal possession thereof.  The issuer seals. - ht
2 CONC tps://lbiiif.riksarkivet.se/sdhk!5281_5281.jpg/full/1000,666/0/default.jpg
2 CONT
2 CONT ==SDHK-nr: [https://sok.riksarkivet.se/?Sokord=Magnus+Gislason&EndastDigitaliserat=false&Fritext=Magnus+Gislason&AvanceradSok=True&FacettFilter=register_facet%24Brev%3a&FacettState=xXo49g%3ac%7c&page=1&postid=sdhk_4279&tab=post#ta
2 CONC b 4279]
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Dating: 1346 March 8'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Sigge Magnusson, Tyrner Mattsson and '''Magnus Gislason''' give Miss Ingeborg Magnusdotter and the nuns in St. Klara Monastery in Stockholm their inheritance castle after Mr Bengt Bosson in Hidinskälf in Husby Ärnevi parish.  The 
2 CONC issuers seal. - https://lbiiif.riksarkivet.se/sdhk!4279_4279.jpg/full/1000,666/0/default.jpg
2 CONT
2 CONT ==SDHK-nr: [https://sok.riksarkivet.se/?Sokord=Magnus+Gislesson+Ulf&EndastDigitaliserat=false&Fritext=Magnus+Gislesson+Ulf&AvanceradSok=True&FacettFilter=register_facet%24Brev%3a&FacettState=xXo49g%3ac%7c&page=1&postid=sdhk_7654&t
2 CONC ab=post#tab 7654]
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Dating: 1360 without a day'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Information on a Thomas Andersson's letter of attachment to Skärplinge village which Ulf Jakobsson received from '''Mr Magnus Gislesson.''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT ==SDHK-nr: [https://sok.riksarkivet.se/?Sokord=Magnus+Gislesson+Ulf&EndastDigitaliserat=false&Fritext=Magnus+Gislesson+Ulf&AvanceradSok=True&FacettFilter=register_facet%24Brev%3a&FacettState=xXo49g%3ac%7c&page=2&postid=sdhk_6954&t
2 CONC ab=post#tab 6954]
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Dating: 1356 January 5, of Issue: Skärplinge'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''The knight Magnus Gislesson''' sells 3 ½ herb teas in Skärplinge (in Österlövsta parish) to Ulf Jacobsson for 110 pounds. The issuer seals. - https://sok.riksarkivet.se/dokument/sdhk/6954.pdf
2 CONT
2 CONT ==SDHK-nr: [https://sok.riksarkivet.se/?Sokord=Magnus+Gislesson+Ulf&EndastDigitaliserat=false&Fritext=Magnus+Gislesson+Ulf&AvanceradSok=True&FacettFilter=register_facet%24Brev%3a&FacettState=xXo49g%3ac%7c&page=3&postid=sdhk_6850&t
2 CONC ab=post#tab 6850]
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Dating: 1355 April 23, of Issue: Tierp Church'''
2 CONT
2 CONT The knight Magnus Gislesson authorizes Mattias in Valla to receive, on his behalf, land on 4 herbal land in Försäter, (Öster) deciduous parish (Olands herald) and then transfer it to Ulf Jacobsson.  The issuer seals. - https://sok
2 CONC .riksarkivet.se/dokument/sdhk/6850.pdf
2 CONT
2 CONT ==SDHK-nr: [https://sok.riksarkivet.se/?ValdSortering=DatumStigande&PageSize=100Sokord=Magnus+Gislesson+Ulf&EndastDigitaliserat=false&FacettFilter=register_facet%24Brev%3a&FacettState=xXo49g%3ac%7c&typAvLista=Standard&AvanceradSok
2 CONC =True&page=6&postid=sdhk_9916&tab=post#tab 9916]
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Dating: 1371 April 15, of Issue: Edsviken'''
2 CONT
2 CONT (Follower of King Albrekt)concludes at Edsviken in Sollentuna the parish and Stockholm castle and city standstill with (supporters of the kings Magnus and Håkan) to apply from this day until the next Pentecost day (1371 25/5) and 
2 CONC then another four weeks, during which termination can, however. be done by open letter, by the latter party in Stockholm, by the former in the opposite camp (at Edsviken). King Albrek's men are named Marshal Karl Ulfson, '''Magnus
2 CONC  Gislesson''' and 8 other knights, Albrekt Grote and 5 other persons representing Stockholm's mayor, council and congregation, and the king's "official" Bo Jonsson, along with 16 other grandparents; the treaty also includes friend
2 CONC s and servants, such as Bishop Thyrgils of Strängnäs, who are now in the city of Stockholm or able to get there, and even those who live elsewhere. On the opposing side, Bishop Nils (Markusson) is named by Linköping, Erik Kättilss
2 CONC on and 9 other knights, as well as Ulf Jonsson and 17 other grandparents; to these come the knights and the savants, the clerks, the merchants, the peasants, and the booksellers, who are in their company or elsewhere. During the s
2 CONC pecified period, the Treaty shall remain in force and unrestricted communication shall prevail. (In addition, the following special provisions :) Even if King Albrekt, his father or their people come to Stockholm, no outcomes will
2 CONC  be made from Stockholm's castle and city, nor will attacks be directed against them to land or water. King Magnus should be treated well and must not be taken away from the city. - https://sok.riksarkivet.se/dokument/sdhk/9916.pd
2 CONC f
2 CONT
2 CONT ==SDHK-nr: [https://sok.riksarkivet.se/?Sokord=Magnus+Gislason&EndastDigitaliserat=false&Fritext=Magnus+Gislason&AvanceradSok=True&FacettFilter=register_facet%24Brev%3a&FacettState=xXo49g%3ac%7c&page=9&postid=sdhk_16751&tab=post#t
2 CONC ab 7298]
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Dating: 1358 January 25, of Issue: Rönö'''
2 CONT
2 CONT The knight Magnus Gislesson and his brother Barnam Gislesson entrust to the reasonable man Olof Bengtsson the management of Barnam's goods and impose on the inhabitants of these to fulfill the obligations pertaining to the goods t
2 CONC o Olof.  The issuers seal. - https://sok.riksarkivet.se/dokument/sdhk/7298.pdf
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://sok.riksarkivet.se/sbl/mobil/Artikel/6228 Sparrow of Aspnäs, Related]
2 CONT
2 CONT Their brother Magnus Gislason(d 1372 or 1373) occurs at the earliest in 1335 and became a knight some of the years 1335–41. When King Magnus 'son Erik rebelled against his father in 1356, M remained loyal to the latter, and in 136
2 CONC 2 King Magnus' son Håkan mentions him among his councils. A letter from 1364, however, testifies that King Magnus deprived him of his estate in Västergötland due to a violation of majesty, and he was subsequently a member of King 
2 CONC Albrek's national council. M dated 1352 letters in his "curia" Örby in Vendel and 1362-70 in Aspnäs, which in 1368 his wife called their "manerium", and whose stone house he bought in 1357 from his half-brother. Except in Västergö
2 CONC tland and Uppland and the neighboring Gästrikland, where he was the first known county governor in 1370, he held land in Västmanland, Närke, Värmland, Östergötland and Småland,
2 CONT
2 CONT In his marriage to the National Council of Knut Folkessons (the family of the Algot Sons ; vol. 1, p. 395 f), Birgitta became M's grandfather to the Swedish National Council and the lawyer Arvid Gustafsson (S of Vik) and the grand
2 CONC father of his daughter Margareta, who owned Örby in 1382, while her sister the National Council. Gotskalk Bengtsson (Ulv) inherited Aspnäs. Margareta Arvidsdotter became married to Ture Bengtsson (Bielke ; bd 4) mother of Sten Tur
2 CONC esson, who in marriage to Karl Ulfssons (Sparre av Tolfta) daughter Margareta became grandfather of Sten Sture dä and grandmother's father to Gustav I.
2 CONT
