1 OCCU Häradshövding, Kommendant, Var på Västerås riksdag 1527 och bevittnade Gustav Vasas testamente, slottsloven
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Mattias Nilsson Kagg=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Son of Nils Mattsson Kagge and Anna Pedersdotter Örnflycht (Nr: 84) 
2 CONT * '''Mattias Nilsson Kagg (son of Nils Mattsson Kagge, Tab. 4), to Fjällskäfte in Floda parish, Södermanland county as well as Kjellstorp in Örslösa parish and Brönas in Härene parish (both in Skaraborg county.).''' Are you includ
2 CONC ed in the length of service for Uppland? 1526-08-10. Witnessed Västerås Riksdag 1527 (Mr.). Received the district court in Skåning's district in Västergötland (GI r.) 1529-10-03, which Torsten Brunsson voluntarily granted to him. 
2 CONC In the castle law on Leckö (GI r.) 1534-02-24 and again (GI r.) 1543-07-25, and (GI r.) 1558-09-12. Signed the inheritance association 1544-01-13, King Gustaf I's will 1560-06-30 and the estates' grant in 1561. Sat ting 1564. On 1
2 CONC 565-04-00 was told of his salvation, because he did not show up for the muster (GI r .). Still alive in 1568. 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT =Married=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Married: [https://www.geni.com/photo/view?album_type=photos_of_me&id=6000000001950346646&photo_id=6000000190555878827&position=0 (1) '''Elin Lindormsdotter (Forstenaätten)'''] daughter of Riksdag Lindorm Brunsson (Forstenasläkte
2 CONC n, no. 2) and Karin Siggesdotter (Sparre).
2 CONT * Married:  [https://www.geni.com/photo/view?album_type=photos_of_me&id=6000000001950346646&photo_id=6000000190555878827&position=0 (2) '''Elin Gustafsdotter (Forstenaätten),'''] in her 1st marriage, who was still alive in 1603 (V
2 CONC ff h. 2-3, p. 124.), daughter of the district chief in Barne district Gustaf Olofsson to Degeberg (Forstenaätten's coat of arms) and Anna Mattsdotter (Katle , No. 70).
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT =Children with Elin Lindormsdotter (1) Marriage=
2 CONT
2 CONT * 1 '''Anna,''' died 1575. Married to the commander at Älvsborg Nils Axelsson Posse , died 1611.
2 CONT * 1. '''Eric,''' Commander at Älvsborg. Died 1592. (Son of Mattias Nilsson Kagg, Tab. 5), to Kjellstorp and Brönas as well as Hålltorp (At (Sch),) dead in Lindärva parish, Skaraborg county. Was King Erik's son-in-law in 1553 (GI r
2 CONC .), received the county chief's letter in Skåning's county in Västergötland (GI r.) 1559-11-10 and the church tithe of Härene priest gäll (GI r.) 11-11-1559. Sealed among the nobility King Gustaf I's will 1560-06-30, and the estat
2 CONC es' grant 1561-04-15. Commanding officer at Älvsborg 1563-04-29, which fortress he surrendered to the Danes on 1563-09-04 after only 13 days of siege, and was therefore sentenced to life by King Erik's committee on 1564-01-06 but 
2 CONC pardoned. Was King Johan III's chamberlain in 1573. Died 1592-07-29 and buried in Härene church, Skaraborg county. Married to Beata Andersdotter, daughter of Riksdag Anders Hansson (Ekeblad ) and Agneta Nilsdotter (crescent) of th
2 CONC e Stola family.
2 CONT * 1. '''Brita,'''  died 1601-12-24 . Married to the castle law and district chief Claes Andersson Ekeblad , died 1614.
2 CONT * 1. '''Nils,''' Duke Carl's chamberlain. Died 1601. (Son of Mattias Nilsson Kagg, Tab. 5), to Kjellstorp and Fjällskäfte as well as Svanseryd in Torestorp parish, Älvsborg county and Styrestad in Lännäs parish, Örebro county. In 
2 CONC 1594 Duke Carls of Södermanland was chamberlain. Signed the decision of the Söderköping Riksdag (Hra.) 1596-01-20. Died 1601-07-29 and buried in Örslösa church, where his tombstone is found. (CJ Ljungström, Kinnefjärdings and Kåll
2 CONC ande härader etc. (1871).) 'He committed murder in 1578, for which, according to King Johan III's letter of 16 March 1579, he was imprisoned, but was then released'. Married 1586-11-06 at Svanseryd to Brita Hård to Svanseryd, born
2 CONC  1563-09-00, died 1630-04-16 at Kjellstorp, daughter of colonel Lars Pedersson Hård (of Segerstad), and Brita Ribbing .
2 CONT * 1. '''Carin,''' died 1605. Married 1st to the master horseman Olof Eriksson Slake , died 1563. Married 2nd to the governor Christoffer Nilsson Ribbing , in his 2nd marriage, died 1602.
2 CONT * 1. '''Linden snake.'''
2 CONT * 1. '''Elin,''' lived in 1598, but died in 1616. Married to the castle law at Gullberg Peder Carlsson Store , in his 2nd marriage
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT =Children with Elin Gustafsdotter, (Forstenaätten) (2) Marriage=
2 CONT
2 CONT * 2. '''Margareta Kagg,''' daughter of prefect Mattias Nilsson Kagg (no. 68) and his 2nd wife Elin Gustafsdotter (Forstenaätten). Married to Peder Bengtsson Svenske (nr. 258).
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT =Links=
2 CONT
2 CONT * http://www.adelsvapen.com/genealogi/Kagg_nr_68#TAB_5
2 CONT * https://www.lansstyrelsen.se/sodermanland/besoksmal/naturreservat/fjellskafte.html
2 CONT * https://sv.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fj%C3%A4llsk%C3%A4fte
2 CONT * http://www.lennheden.com/genealogi/gunnar/000/0001/183.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT =Sources=
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT * Fick häradsrätten i Skånings härad i Västergötland (G I r.) 1529-10-03, som Torsten  Brunsson självvilligt upplåtit åt honom. I slottsloven på Leckö (G I r.) 1534-02-24 och ånyo (G I r.) 1543-07-25, och (G I r.) 1558-09-12. 
2 CONT * '''Mats Kagg''' samt hans barns arv efter deras mödrar hustru ''[https://www.geni.com/people/Elin-Lindormsdotter-Forstena/6000000003275920163 'Elin Lindormsdotter (Vinge)]''' och hustru '''Anna Torstensdotter''', Sven Tysk till 
2 CONC Alarp (Rosenquist), Olof Drake till Intorp, Lasse Bröms till Borrarp, Torbjörn Kettilsson i Torp, Anders Krabbe (sammandrag) ref: [https://sok.riksarkivet.se/?Sokord=torstensdotter&EndastDigitaliserat=false&AvanceradSok=False&page
2 CONC =24&postid=Arkis+426D7D32-807D-440C-B8FC-7CE5ABC672A3&tab=post&FacettState=undefined%3Ac%7C#tab Frälsemännens egna längder]
2 CONT * 1545 17/6. Mälsåker. Brev om jordaskifte mellan '''Mats Kagg''', Lorens Mattson å sin hustrus vägnar och Hans Kyle å sin hustrus vägnar. [Pergament- och pappersbrevsamlingen nr 37] ref: https://sok.riksarkivet.se/?Sokord=mats+ka
2 CONC gg&EndastDigitaliserat=false&AvanceradSok=False&page=1&postid=Arkis+F8B0A25E-779F-11D5-A6F2-0002440207BB&tab=post&FacettState=undefined%3Ac%7C#tab
2 CONT * GEDCOM Note - Historia[redigera | redigera wikitext]Fjällskäfte omnämndes första gången 1399. Under cirka 200 år gick egendomen i arv inom släkten Kagg. Bland annat bodde fältmarskalken, riksmarsken med mera Lars Kagg (1595-1661
2 CONC ) här. 1680 indrogs egendomen till kronan genom Karl XI:s reduktion. Det blev dock snart enskild egendom igen och kom 1782 i friherre G. Celsings ägo. Senare tillföll Fjällskäfte släkten Ihre som fideikommiss, men återgick genom g
2 CONC ifte 1865 till släkten Celsing. 1925 var Herman von Celsing ägare av Fjällskäfte. Fjällskäfte gods ägs ännu (2008) inom släkten von Celsing.
