2 CONT * Parents: Harald Stensson [Gren] (- 1457) Sigrid Tomasdotter [von Vitzen] (- 1461) 
2 CONT * Cecilia Haraldsdotter (Gren), the birth and death year unknown (still lived in 1465), was a Swedish nobility lady. She was the daughter of Harald Stensson Gren and Sigrid Tomasdotter van Vitzen and her niece of the Magnus Gren C
2 CONC ouncil. She also became Grandma's mother of Gustav Vasa.
2 CONT * Cecilia Haraldsdotter had a street in Sigtuna , Cecilia Haraldsdotter's street , named after her.
2 CONT * Buried: : Skånela kyrka, Uppland 1) 
2 CONT
2 CONT =Married=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Married:  July 5, 1441 [1] with the national council of '''Eskil Isaksson Banér.''' She then received Venngarn's "farm and estate" with several subordinate farms (including Stora Brännbo) in the morning gift of her husband. In t
2 CONC he letter of gift, two of the most powerful men of the time, Karl Knutsson (Bonde) and Bengt Jönsson (Oxenstierna), appear in their capacity as a resident.  Cecilia Haraldsdotter has been given a street in Sigtuna, Cecilia Haralds
2 CONC dotter's street, named after him. [4] 
2 CONT
2 CONT =Children=
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Sigrid Eskilsdotter (Banner),''' Sigrid Eskilsdotter (Banér) , born in the second half of the 15th century on Lindholm's farm , died in the fall of 1527 in Gäddeholm , [ 1 ] was a Swedish noble lady . In her first marriage sh
2 CONC e gave birth to daughter Cecilia Månsdotter (Eka) who became the mother of King Gustav Vasa . Sigrid Eskilsdotter Banér thus became grandmother to the king. In her second marriage was born the daughter Kristina Gyllenstierna who m
2 CONC arried the governor and the governor Sten Sture the younger .
2 CONT * '''Knut Eskilsson (Banner),''' He was the son of the knight and the national council Eskil Isaksson (Banér) and his first wife Cecilia Haraldsdotter (Gren) , and older half-brother to the national council Nils Eskilsson (Banér) 
2 CONC and brother of Sigrid Eskilsdotter (Banér) . Riksråd 1476-1515, lawman in the law of Västmanland and Dalarna , Västergötland law and Uppland law . Dubbed the knight by King Hans coronation in the Great Church in Stockholm November
2 CONC  26, 1497. Hövitsman 1517 in Stockholm.
2 CONT
