1 OCCU Riksdrots, jordmagnat
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * Bo Jonsson (Grip) (early 1330s – 20 August 1386) was head of the royal council and marshal under the regency of Magnus IV of Sweden. Also in the council was his friend and colleague, Karl Ulfsson av Ulvåsa, eldes
2 CONC t son of Saint Birgitta. From 1369, during Albert of Sweden’s reign, he was Officialis Generalis (the king's highest official) and from 1371 Lord High Steward (drots in Swedish).
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://sok.riksarkivet.se/?Sokord=Bo+Jonsson+Grip&EndastDigitaliserat=false&AvanceradSok=False&page=7&postid=sdhk_11928&tab=post SDHK no: 11928]
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Dating: 1381 June 28, Place of issue: Nyköping''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Bo Jonsson , Drots in Sweden''', announces in an open letter that he has confiscated all of Karl Nilsson's property in Södermanland due to the large and varied crimes he has been convicted of, which is widely known in Sweden. T
2 CONC hese properties have not been obtained by the issuer either by purchase or exchange or in any other way from Gregers Anundsson or his wife Ingeborg Nilsdotter. The issuer therefore certifies that these have neither inheritance nor
2 CONC  debts after Karl Nilsson. Furthermore, the issuer has sold to Gregers, his wife Ingeborg and their heirs and in perpetuity 1 markland of land with all appurtenances in Viggeby in Dalby parish in Hagunda county, which he received 
2 CONC from bishop Tord (Gunnarsson) in Strängnäs. The issuer fully acknowledges having received the purchase price (from the buyers) and divests himself and his heirs of the property and transfers it to Gregers Anundsson and Ingeborg Ni
2 CONC lsdotter and their heirs with full right of disposition. He gives the head of the district in the same district where the property is located a power of attorney to give a lease to the buyers or their representatives.
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://sok.riksarkivet.se/bildvisning/Sdhk_11928_11928.jpg#?c=&m=&s=&cv=&xywh=-128%2C-264%2C4622%2C3438 '''The issuer seals together with the knights Karl Ulfsson of Tofta and Knut Karlsson.''']
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Sources:''' Original:  Orig. on perg. (28.7 x 13.4 cm, fold 1.4 cm; 18 lines), Sv. The National Archives (SE/RA/0101)  images Post-medieval transcripts:  Brocman: II Misc. 24:11; (circa 1700) Biographica G 11 b: Grip RA
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://sok.riksarkivet.se/?Sokord=Bo+Jonsson+Grip&EndastDigitaliserat=false&AvanceradSok=False&page=19&postid=sdhk_13034&tab=post SDHK no: 13034]
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Dating: 1386 January 13, Place of issue: Old town''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT Lars in Forsby (V. Ed's son) sells to, '''Bo Jonsson, drots''' in Sweden 3 acres of land in Flugenäs in Dalhem's parish in [N.] Tjust's district for 12 öre Swedish money. This was done in county council in Västervik. 12 fasts are 
2 CONC enumerated. On the back, signature of Margareta Grip: "her Boo".
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Sources:''' Original:  Or. perg. Sjöholm archive RA 0107.13, Post-medieval regest/notice:  Reg. Vretstorp L 31, ULA, Photocopy:  DK
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://sok.riksarkivet.se/?Sokord=Bo+Jonsson+Grip&EndastDigitaliserat=false&AvanceradSok=False&page=21&postid=sdhk_12608&tab=post SDHK no: 12608]
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Dating: 1384 March 12, Place of issue: Nyköping''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT Finvid Finvidsson trades to '''Bo Jonsson, drots in Sweden''', Nynäs with mill and eel fishing, land in Oppeby, Grinda, Ö. and V. Segersta etc. in Bälinge parish, Stångby in Tystberga parish, Hamra in Bogsta parish, Huseby and Eke
2 CONC by in Råby parish, Ökna in Torsåkers parish, etc. in Rönö district as well as land in Fors parish in Västerrekarne and in Vallby parish in Österrekarne etc. the estates that Bo Jonsson owned in Lidingö in the parish of Danderyd an
2 CONC d ships, etc. as well as in Stockeby and Skärsätra etc. in Solna parish.
