1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Märta Bosdotter=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Daughter of Bo Stensson, till Bergunda (Natt och Dag) and Katarina Svensdotter Sture 
2 CONT
2 CONT =Married=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Married: '''Peter Arvidsson Ribbing,''' in 1388 in Swedenmap son of Arvid Sigvidsson Ribbing 
2 CONT
2 CONT =Children=
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Knut Arvidsson Ribbing,''' till Svanserid, married 
2 CONT * '''Ea Arvidsdottor,''' married Broder Svensson (Tjurhufvud eller Somme
2 CONT * '''Peter Arvidsson Ribbing,''' married Kjertstin Gostafsdotter
2 CONT * '''Niels Arvidsson Ribbing,''' Lefde 1449.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://sok.riksarkivet.se/sbl/Mobil/Artikel/6656 Ribbing, Relatives, by Swedish Biographical Dictionary]
2 CONT
2 CONT Sigvid Bengtsson and Knut Sigvidssons aforementioned related to Mark's district in Västergötland may indicate a close relationship with the first known district chief there, Knut R (d earliest 1417), who is mentioned as such in 14
2 CONC 15. He had in 1402 sealed a market letter together with Peder R(d earliest 1414) and a knight Lindorm R who is not mentioned in life later. It has been claimed (DAA; Hildebrand) that they were brothers, but there is no evidence fo
2 CONC r this. Since Peder R is mentioned in the letter 1402 before Lindorm R, although he had the title of knight, it seems rather as if Peder was the father of Lindorm and Knut (Liljeholm), especially as the latter could not be substan
2 CONC tiated until the 1390s, while Peder R may be identical with the person or persons with this name that appears as early as 1355 and 1364. He is probably also identical with the person who in King Olof's only in transcripts known ha
2 CONC ndwriting 1377 is called Petrus Aaselson  - or Axelsson  -  dictus Rybbing , which combined (DAA; Elgenstierna ; Mohlin) with that of an Ascerus Magni(d earliest 1351) carried the family R's coat of arms and had a brother named Si
2 CONC gvid; in the 1390s, Peder and Knut R sealed for Peter Prika's widow Ingeborg Sigvidsdotter (d earliest 1413), who also carried the family R's coat of arms and was therefore presumed (Liedgren) to have been the daughter of Sigvid M
2 CONC agnusson.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''The district chief Knut Ribbing was probably (Hildebrand 1961) father-in-law of the knight Broder Svensson (vol. 6) and father of Peder R (d earliest 1474), who was district chief in Mark from some of the years 1442–59 and prob
2 CONC ably until his death. He came to prepare the social advancement of his descendants by marrying Councilor Bo Stensson's (Night and Day ; vol. 26) daughter Märta. Their son Knut R(d earliest 1512) was warlord in Mark at least from 1
2 CONC 484 until his death.''' His manor was probably Svansjö in Torestorp in this district, which he states to be his farm, when he issued a letter there in 1493, and he sealed a letter there in 1497. As early as 1402, the aforementione
2 CONC d knight Lindorm R had dated a letter there. Knut R's seal is the first in which the R-weapon's nautical blade has received its current appearance, ie with the tips upwards and provided with a shaft (Raneke; cf. Hildebrand, p. 163
2 CONC  f). 
2 CONT
2 CONT =Links=
2 CONT
2 CONT * https://www.adelsvapen.com/genealogi/Natt_och_Dag_nr_13#TAB_12
2 CONT * https://www.adelsvapen.com/genealogi/Ribbing_nr_15#TAB_1
2 CONT
2 CONT =Sources=
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''von Nackreij - Skytte, Volume 3,page 371''' - https://books.google.com/books?id=8nbUjE7AsQYC&pg=PA371&lpg=PA371&dq=Sigurd+Erlingsson+Ribbing&source=bl&ots=LJf2rHeJEI&sig=ACfU3U0cWteNZbilMREEbENWgoJVG9fL3g&hl=en&sa=X&ved=2ahUK
2 CONC EwiTt6_jg9DpAhWSu54KHTvABT8Q6AEwGnoECAMQAQ#v=onepage&q=Sigurd%20Erlingsson%20Ribbing&f=false
2 CONT
