1 OCCU Lagman i Tiohärad, Riddare, Rådman, Kammarmästare Lagman i Tiohärad, Riksråd, Kammarmästare, Lagman
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Ture Kettilsson (Bielke)=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Son of Kettil (ancestor Bielke)
2 CONT * Chamber Master, Knight, Council of Ministers
2 CONT * Death between 1322/27, Band 04 (1924), page 144
2 CONT
2 CONT =Married=
2 CONT
2 CONT Ture Kettilsson, , Deceased before 1327-02-29. Knights and national council. The man in Värend. '''Married to Sigrid (sparrow),''' possibly daughter of Ulf Abjörnsson (sparrow) known to King Magnus Eriksson's time.  Ture K was '''
2 CONC Married twice, the other wife was the daughter of Nils Sigridsson (Natt og Dag).''' Generi domini Boonis Nicolai erant dominus Thorirus Catilli et Haquinus Lää", i.e. in pure Swedish: Bo Nilsson's (Night and Day) brother-in-law..T
2 CONC ure Kettilsson (Bielke) and Håkan (Jonsson) Läma.
2 CONT
2 CONT =Children=
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Erik Turesson,''' Privy Council. Died about 1328. Knights and national council. Married before 1315 to Margareta Bengtsdotter (? Folkungaätten ).
2 CONT * '''Nils Dannes Turesson,''' Knight. Knight. Married 1: o 1325 to Ingeborg Larsdotter . Married 2: o with Katarina Pedersdotter (Bååt) , daughter of the knight and national council Peder Jonsson ( Bååt ) and Kristina Hemmingsdott
2 CONC er ( Tanne ).
2 CONT * '''Sten Turesson,''' Marsk. Died 1350. appears in documents 1334. Arms still 1341-09-29, but was knight 1343-07-08 . Was Counsel 1348 and is called Marsh 1348. Dead 1350 before 15/9. He accompanied King Magnus on his Russian cam
2 CONC paign and seems to have been left at the king's return as the commander of the Swedish troops and was in Reval on 1349-04-00. (Bbl.). Married 1345 to Ingeborg Nilsdotter (Sparre) in her 1st marriage (married 2nd before 1360 with t
2 CONC he knight Bengt Nilsson ( Oxenstierna ), died about 1371], died before 1377-07-11 daughter of the knight, the Swedish Council and the Nils Abjörnsson (Sparre) to Salsta and Ängsö, and Bengta Abrahamsdotter.
2 CONT * '''Nils Turesson,''' Council of Ministers and drots. Died 1364. to Kråkerum in Mönsterås parish, Kalmar county. Was a layman on Öland 1339-10-13 and called gunner 1341. Became knight in 1342, national council 1344 and slain 1344
2 CONC . Team in Tiohärad in Småland 1348-1356. Ånyo was defeated in 1349-1351 and in this capacity led the board in Sweden under King Magnus Eriksson's second campaign against the Russians 1350-51. Was the Sword of Sweden (Treaties of S
2 CONC weden 2 p. 203.) 1355-10-24. Struggled between King Magnus and his son Erik on Erik's side. Chief magistrate of Finland 1357. Was King Erik's king (Rosman, Bjärka-Särby.) 1358-04-09. Lawman of Finland and still held this dignity 1
2 CONC 362-02-15. One of the Swedish envoys who made peace with the Hanseatic cities of Lübeck in 1361 and shortly thereafter in Greifswald on behalf of Sweden entered into a covenant. Once again (Black Book of Turku Cathedral, no. 178).
2 CONC  ) 1362-05-23 and one of the foremost in the league of great men, who stamped against the king, why he was banished to the other treacherous gentlemen in 1363. Returned with Albrekt of Mecklenburg and became for the fifth (sixth) 
2 CONC time in 1364, and received for its services Viborg castle and county. Death in the fall of 1364 during King Albrekt's siege of Turku Castle. Married 1st before 1339 (Rosman Bjärka-Säby.) WithIngrid Sunesdotter, daughter of the kni
2 CONC ght and the Swedish Council Sune Jonsson ( Bååt ) and his 1st wife Karin Henriksdotter Glysing. Married 2nd before 1348 with Margareta Mattsdotter (sparrow). Married 3rd possibly already in 1351 with Sigrid Håkansdotter (2 turned 
2 CONC sparrows), who was still living 1371-11-09 in her (2nd?) Marriage (married possibly 1st with the knight and the national council Knut Folkesson (seizure head), dead about 1349. Married 3: o? (2: o) with Vohad Drekow).
2 CONT * '''Margareta Turesdotter,''' Deceased before 1380-06-03. Married in 1336 with the knight Karl Magnusson ( Örnfot ).
2 CONT * '''Ramfrid Turesdotter,''' Deceased before 1348. Married to NN.
2 CONT * '''Bengt Turesson,''' Privy Council. Squire. Privy Council. Mentioned between the years 1341-1358. Married to Ingeborg Magnusdotter (lion) in her 1st marriage [married 2: o to Earl Erengisle Sunesson ( Bååt ), died 1392], buried
2 CONC  in Vadstena 1390-06-28, daughter of the knight Magnus Gudmarsson ( Ulvåsaätten ) and Karin Birgersdotter ( Finstaätten ).
2 CONT * '''Helena Turesdotter,''' Married to the knight and the Council of Staff Staffan Röriksson (The Family of the Sons of Staffans ).
2 CONT
2 CONT == [https://sok.riksarkivet.se/sbl/Mobil/Artikel/8773#/sbl/Mobil/Artikel/18188 Ture Kettilsson (Bielke)Swedish, by Biographical Dictionary] 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Chamber Master, Knight, Council of Ministers, by the Swedish Biographical Dictionary'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Ture Kettilsson (Bielke) is mentioned for the first time on July 13, 1283 as a participant in the Grand Meeting, which Magnus Ladulås convened in Hälgö, and was already a knight. Three years later (May 22, 1286) he proved a new su
2 CONC ch meeting in Stockholm; first Sept 11 In 1288, however, he is explicitly referred to as the Council of Ministers. After King Magnus' death, he took part in the guardianship of the young Birger Magnusson. Since Birger himself took
2 CONC  over the government, T. appears to have been in favor of him for a long time to come. He thus became (most recently 1310) the king's chamberlain (camerarius) - one of the first with this title in our claims - and in letters of 13
2 CONC 13 and 1315 he also appears as a layman in Tiohärad's (Värends) law. It seems, however, as if lately a breakup has occurred between the king and his confidant; perhaps T. has finally approached the ducal party, in whose direction 
2 CONC his eldest son Erik(see below 2) were. In any event, some time before his fall, King Birger occupied the chamberlain's office with another person, Peder Andersson, who is his camerarius Feb. 27. 1318. Even from the team's order, T
2 CONC . was discharged, probably already during Birger's reign: in 1319 Tuke Jonsson is a layman in Tiohärad. T. participated in the young Magnus Erikssonselection to king July 8, 1319 and then diligently attended the council meetings d
2 CONC uring the new regime in the years 1320-22. In the latter year he entered the Grand Confederate Confederation in Skara (July 20) directed against the widow of Ingeborg (July 20), but then his name disappears from the sources, and i
2 CONC n 1327 he is mentioned as dead. - Where T. had his seat, is completely unknown, but as he seals on several occasions issued in Kalmar, it is not excluded that he already owned Kråkerum, which in any case in 1343 seems to have been
2 CONC  in the family's possession and in 1350, according to judgment, was inhabited by T's son Drotsen Nils Turesson(see below 4). T's wife was called Sigrid and survived him. According to the old genealogist Utter, who had seen one of 
2 CONC her sealed, now lost letter of the year 1327, she carried a spar in the gun; the task can possibly be regarded as confirmed by the fact that T's sons were evidently related to Ulf Abjörnsson (sparrow) known to King Magnus Eriksson
2 CONC 's time.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Source''' [https://sok.riksarkivet.se/sbl/Mobil/Artikel/8773#/sbl/Mobil/Artikel/18188Swedish Biographical Dictionary] 
2 CONT
2 CONT ==SDHK-nr: [https://sok.riksarkivet.se/?Sokord=ture+kettilsson+l%c3%a4ma&EndastDigitaliserat=false&AvanceradSok=False&page=1&postid=sdhk_2338&tab=post#tab 2338]
2 CONT
2 CONT * Dating, 1310 March 5, of Issue: Elsinore
2 CONT
2 CONT King Birger of Sweden gives the letterman Mr Folke Jonsson and his heirs his estate "Algö" with all the best wishes as thanks for his many services. Sealants are the issuer, King E (rich) of Denmark, and King Birger's Councilors B
2 CONC ishop Magnus in Växjö, the lord Leonard, the '''treasurer Ture Kettilsson,''' Marshal Håkan Läma, Mr Knut Jonsson, Mr Tuke Jonsson, Mr Peter Likvidsson, Mr Tore ('Törirus') Birgersson, Mr Håkan Haraldsson and Mr Holmvid Elifsson. 
2 CONC - https://sok.riksarkivet.se/dokument/sdhk/2338.pdf
2 CONT
2 CONT * SEAL, 2 of 11 (12?) Ripped off; According to the drawing, the seal N. 6 and 8 had been undamaged, the other 9 gone.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==SDHK-nr: [https://sok.riksarkivet.se/?Sokord=ture+kettilsson+l%c3%a4ma&EndastDigitaliserat=false&AvanceradSok=False&page=2&postid=sdhk_2479&tab=post#tab 2479]
2 CONT
2 CONT * Dating: 1312 February 20, of Issue: Stegeborg
2 CONT
2 CONT King Birger of Sweden, the king Knut Jonsson, Folke Jonsson, Marshal Håkan Läma, '''Ture Kettilsson,''' Tuke Jonsson, Rörik Birgersson in place of the late Mr Leonard, the knights Peter Likvidsson and Håkan Haraldsson as well as t
2 CONC he weapons Torsten Gudvastsson, Stefan Röriksson, Jedvard Filess Karl Turesson, Kettil Puke, Karl Orestesson, Birger Jonsson, Martin "Houære", Konrad "Ysern" and Magnus Sibbessonannounces and acknowledges that they are jointly ind
2 CONC ebted to King Erik of Denmark 2000 marks of silver, cologne weight, which should have been paid on the coming day of John the Baptist, but which, by advancing the due date, should now instead be paid to King Erik or his heirs near
2 CONC est coming mickels mass. Furthermore, King Birger promises to set himself up in Söderköping and the kings Folke Jonsson, Knut Jonsson and other knights and arms to set up in Roskilde, Denmark, if the said sum of silver had not bee
2 CONC n repaid to King Erik or his heirs on the above due date, and that not Leave these places, until the debt is resolved. In addition, King Birger promises to replace each of the aforementioned knights and gunmen, who would die befor
2 CONC e the silver was repaid, with another equivalent knight or gunner.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==SDHK-nr: [https://sok.riksarkivet.se/?Sokord=Ture+Kettilsson&EndastDigitaliserat=false&AvanceradSok=False&page=2&postid=sdhk_3085&tab=post&FacettState=undefined%3Ac%7C#tab 3085]
2 CONT
2 CONT * Dating: 1321 April 12, of Issue: Örebro
2 CONT
2 CONT The bishops, Karl i Linköping och Israel i Västerås, Knut Jonsson, Filip Ulfsson, '''Ture Kettilsson,''' Knut Magnusson, Stefan Röriksson, Erik Turesson, Peter Likvidsson, Bo Nilsson, Hemming Odgisleson, Sigmund Erengisleson, Tord
2 CONC  Bonde, Gisle Elinason, Jon Nilsson, Nils Abjörnsson, Gustav Tunason, Jon Tolfsson, Sigmund Kieldorsson, Ragnvald Magnusson.  Ulf Saxesson would have been imprisoned by the action of some Swedes, explaining that they considered th
2 CONC is incredible, but suspected that this might have been perpetrated by some youngsters or strangers from Varberg. Since they strongly disapprove of this, they insist that the Norwegian Council had to request in writing to the King'
2 CONC s mother, Duchess Ingeborg, that she wanted to remedy all things that might disturb the calm of her son's kingdoms, and in such matters rather listen to mature and experienced men than to young people. and strangers' advice. - htt
2 CONC ps://sok.riksarkivet.se/dokument/sdhk/3085.pdf
2 CONT
2 CONT ==SDHK-nr: [https://sok.riksarkivet.se/?Sokord=Ture+Kettilsson&EndastDigitaliserat=false&AvanceradSok=False&page=17&postid=sdhk_1535&tab=post&FacettState=undefined%3Ac%7C#tab 1535]
2 CONT
2 CONT * Dating: 1292 without a day
2 CONT
2 CONT Karl Gustavsson draws up his will; to the preaching brethren in Skänninge, from whom he chooses his burial ground, he donates 10 marks of soldered silver, which shall be required by former Bishop B. of Linköping, who owes them the
2 CONC  issuer, to redeem from the crusade promise he further donates 80 marks solderly and to the sister monastery in Skänninge his farm in "budhams" on condition that Sister Katarina in the monastery may dispose of the return of the fa
2 CONC rm during her lifetime. He also gives various sums of money to various brother and sister conventions in Västerås, Eskilstuna, Strängnäs, Enköping, Fogdö (Vårfruberga), Sko, Östra Aros, Turku, “dynæmunæ” (Dünamunde?), Reval, Visby
2 CONC  and Gotland in general. Finally, he donates money, ransom, etc. to Prior Abraham, Peter "Stikkæ" or his heirs, Elof from "summary", Knut Jonsson, Agmund Dotersson, Agmund 'who is with Mr Bengt Petersson', his sister Ingeborg, Dot
2 CONC er, Ragnfrid, Hemming Isaksson's wife, Gertrud "Olafs", Hemming Djäknes's wife, Sigrid, Helena, Kristina, her priest Luscius, Elof Botulfsson, custodian Ingrid from "lächiu" , Elof "dreggiæbassæ", Tord "gauze", Öar "Wafræ", Johann
2 CONC es Aggesson, Johannes "stekar", Elof Brodersson, Martin, Ingevast, Bagge, Sigge Fant, Jakob Svensk, Ragvald and Ragvald "atha". Bishop L. in Linköping, Mr. Svantepolk, Mr. Nils Sigridsson, '''Mr. Torir (Ture) Kettilsson''' and Mr.
2 CONC  Magnus Kristineson, who are also sealed together with the issuer, are appointed as testament executors. Tord "gauze", Islands "Wafræ", Johannes Aggesson, Johannes "roast", Elof Brodersson, Martin, Ingevast, Bagge, Sigge Fant, Jak
2 CONC ob Swedish, Ragvald and Ragvald "atha". Bishop L. in Linköping, Mr. Svantepolk, Mr. Nils Sigridsson, Mr. Torir (Ture) Kettilsson and Mr. Magnus Kristineson, who are also sealed together with the issuer, are appointed as testament 
2 CONC executors. Tord "gauze", Islands "Wafræ", Johannes Aggesson, Johannes "roast", Elof Brodersson, Martin, Ingevast, Bagge, Sigge Fant, Jakob Swedish, Ragvald and Ragvald "atha". Bishop L. in Linköping, Mr. Svantepolk, Mr. Nils Sigri
2 CONC dsson, '''Mr. Torir (Ture) Kettilsson''' and Mr. Magnus Kristineson, who are also sealed together with the issuer, are appointed as testament executors. - https://sok.riksarkivet.se/dokument/sdhk/1535.pdf
2 CONT
2 CONT ==SDHK-nr: [https://sok.riksarkivet.se/?Sokord=Ture+Kettilsson&EndastDigitaliserat=false&Fritext=Ture+Kettilsson&AvanceradSok=True&page=8&postid=sdhk_1870&tab=post&FacettState=undefined%3Ac%7C#tab 1870]
2 CONT
2 CONT * Dating: 1300 without a day 
2 CONT
2 CONT Orm Karlsson announces that he has sold to '''Ture Kettilsson''' and in his ownership the estate in "sterikæløso" in Vista inherited which he (Orm) inherited after all his father, and he now transfers to him and his heirs the full
2 CONC  ownership and the right of disposal of the said goods. - https://sok.riksarkivet.se/dokument/sdhk/1870.pdf
2 CONT
2 CONT The issuer seals. - https://www.geni.com/photo/view/6000000003900292015?album_type=photos_of_me&photo_id=6000000140199059913
2 CONT
