2 CONT
2 CONT =Cecilia Olsdotter=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Cecilia Olsdotter. Still alive in 1479. Married to Sven Pik, who cannot be dated later than 1462. Remarried no later than 1479 to the district chief Philippus Karlsson ( Mälsåkerätten ) at Mälsåker in Ytterselö sn, Selebo hd in 
2 CONC Södermanland, who was still alive on 14.12.1497.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://www.adelsvapen.com/genealogi/Stenbock,_%C3%A4ldre_%C3%A4tten Capricorn, Older Family]
2 CONT
2 CONT Olof Jönsson (son of Jösse skytte, tab. 1). Earliest mentioned in 1406. Became between 1408 and 2.2 1426 district chief in Sunnerbo hd in Småland, which he was still 17.3 1445; no successor can be appointed until several years aft
2 CONC er his death; it is probably a misspelling, as on 6.5 1442 he is called Hövitsman in Sunnerbo. Mentioned among the council and men of the kingdom as early as 1435, but as a councilor only in 1440. Dated 1406 letter on his father's
2 CONC  former manor Ekomarp in Berga sn, Sunnerbo hd, but had at least 4.9 1444 and 8.6 1451 as manor Erikstad in Vittaryds sn in the same hd. Was burned, probably during the war in 1455. In 1441 was widowed by Sestrid, daughter of the 
2 CONC knight Knut Eringisleson ( Barun ) also called Knut April and Bengta Matsdotter (star). Remarried to Margareta Svensdotter ( Krumme ), who still lived on 26.2 1484 at Sunnaryd in Bolmsö sn, Västbo hd, was the daughter of Sven Bäk 
2 CONC and Botild Klausdotter ( Apellegard ) and remarried Christiern Drake.
2 CONT
2 CONT =Children=  
2 CONT
2 CONT * 1. '''Jösse Olsson,''' 1441, died 1488, courtier, councillor. See tab. 3 .
2 CONT * 1. '''Gustav Olsson,''' 1441, died 1492, knight, councillor. See tab. 4 .
2 CONT * 1. Knut Olsson or Knut April. Enrolled in Nov. 1437 at the University of Rostock and in the winter of 1439 at the University of Leipzig, where he became a bachelor in the summer of 1440 and a master in the spring of 1442. Became
2 CONC  a canon in Uppsala on 30.4.1445 at the latest. Was 8.3 1449 canon in both Uppsala and Linköping and vicar in Stockholm, ordained 18.3 s.å. to deacon and 12.4. so. to priest. Resigned from the vicarship between 25.1 1451 and 1453.
2 CONC  Died between 1455 and 1475. He had an illegitimate son named Olof).
2 CONT * 1. '''Eringisl Olsson.''' Died no earlier than 1441.
2 CONT * 2. '''Anund Olsson.''' Died childless.
2 CONT * 2. '''Cecilia Olsdotter.''' Still alive in 1479. Married to Sven Pik, who cannot be dated later than 1462. Remarried no later than 1479 to the district chief Philippus Karlsson ( Mälsåkerätten ) at Mälsåker in Ytterselö sn, Sele
2 CONC bo hd in Södermanland, who was still alive on 14.12.1497.
2 CONT * 2. '''Claus Olsson.''' Probably identical to the person with this name whom King Karl Knutsson sent to Roslagen in 1469 to gather people against Erik Karlsson's ( Vasa ) rebellion, but who was beaten and captured by him at Knutb
2 CONC y church. In that case, became a knight between 1469 and 1471.
2 CONT * 2. '''Märta Olsdotter.''' Still alive 12.3 1486 and was then married to Jöns Persson ( Ulfsax ), who then had Håringe in Bolmsö sn, Västbo hd as a seat farm and was still alive in 1488.
2 CONT * 2. '''Estrid Olsdotter.''' Died unmarried.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://sok.riksarkivet.se/?Sokord=Sven+Pik&EndastDigitaliserat=false&AvanceradSok=False&page=2&postid=sdhk_28343&tab=post SDHK-nr: 28343]
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''1465 more'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Cecilia (Olofsdotter), also after Sven Pik, with two 'brother' riddaren Gustav Olsson (Stenbock) went for liquid for gods in Holland, som hon och hennes and salt till honor.
2 CONT
