2 CONT
2 CONT If his mother is estimated to have been born 1490, then it seems unlikely Fleming's estimated d.o.b. of 1535 is correct.  Perhaps 1520 is a better estimate.
2 CONT
2 CONT -As Joakim his OLDER brother was definitely born 1534, 1535 would be his earliest birthdate.
2 CONT
2 CONT He had at least three other children with unknown mothers, not mentioned here:
2 CONT
2 CONT Gottskalk - by unknown mother;   Karl b circa 1559  - 1596  Studied at Rostock Sept 1594 Filippa date unknown.  Married Johan Jönsson.  Visited Johan Fleming in prison, leading up to his execution 1599.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT Gustaf, † 1583 at Rydboholm. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Erik, † young, buried in Parga's church (30). 
2 CONT
2 CONT Katarina, † 1649% Married 1620 n / 6 at  Strömsholm, when Queen Katarina Stenbock held the  wedding, with Erik Klasson Bjelke, frier,  (frih. N 8). She compiled about her  brother Johans fate a written story that. 1643,  and the i
2 CONC ssue in the first band of Loenboms  Anec dots about Swedish men. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Johan, b. 1578. Chamber King of King  Sigismund in Poland, where he traveled 1597/6 (38).  Followed the king to Sweden in 1598 and participated in  the feudes that arose on his arrival, as well as  in his hasty return to Poland, b
2 CONC ut  still came to Finland in the fall for Finland for  individual affairs. Stayed on his farm  Qvidja in Pargas. Attended the fall of 1599 in Turku's  defense against Duke Karl, after the castle 
2 CONT
2 CONT was detained and 1599 10 / n in Turku.  Buried in Turku Cathedral 14 / n, where was called  with all bells. - Envy. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Hebla, † 1639 V2 on Tuna in Sweden. Married  1615 23/8 in Stockholm with Peder Banér Council  (frih. n: r 22), † 1644. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Margareta, buried 1599 in Stockholm's  Storkyrka, Breed of 1598 from her to the brother  Johan, is preserved in Sv. National Archives (27). Unmarried. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Gottskalk Klasson (f. The marriage, of  unknown mother), chambermaid, abducted 1591. See  Gottskalk Klasson's family. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Karl, (f. Except the marriage of unknown mother),  student in Rostock 1594/9, is called in the record:  Carolus Nicolai Flemingius (37); - † 1596 in  Turku, buried with all bells. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Olof Klasson, (f. Except the marriage, of  unknown mother). The prisoner of the Turku castle,  together with half-brother Johan Fleming. By correction of  Duke Charles's order 15991Ü / n, buried 12 / n  in Turku cathedral. Johan F
2 CONC leming, in his  resignation letter to the mother, when he thought that Olof  Klasson would be forgiven to life, that she wanted to  declare his credentials "that they were  my dear cry. Former father deceased,  may not have been d
2 CONC efeated. "(38) 
2 CONT
2 CONT Filippa Klasdotter (except for the marriage  of unknown mother). Married to Johan  Joens son (38). Half-brother Johan Fleming step two  days before his execution to his mother and daughter  she remembers Filippa and her husband,  
2 CONC who in all ways assisted him in his  captivity and promised to control his funeral.  http://runeberg.org/frfinl/0126.html
2 CONT
