1 NAME Åke /Jönsson Svarte Skåning/
2 GIVN Åke
2 _MARNM Jönsson Svarte Skåning
2 NICK Svarte Åke
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE BEF 1430
1 DEAT
2 DATE 1494
1 OCCU Riddare lagman
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Svarte Åke Jönsson=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Son of Jöns Nilsson Skåning and Ingeborg Nilsdotter (Natt och Dag)
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://www.adelsvapen.com/genealogi/Svarte_Sk%C3%A5ning Adelsvapen Geneologies Skåning]
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT '''TABLE 5'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Answered Åke Jönsson .''' Said to be 60 years old in 1477, although he is mentioned in letters after his brother Ture, who was described as 50 years old in 1477. Probably identical to the "Swarte Akow" which in 1438 together wi
2 CONC th Swedes was enrolled at the University of Leipzig. Appears in Sweden at the earliest in 1440. Was knighted between 1446 and 19.1 1449, so apparently at King Karl's coronation in Uppsala 29.6 1448. Was a councilor at least from 1
2 CONC 450 and is mentioned as a nobleman at Ringstadaholm 19.1 1451 and 1453. In 1454 he received a deed of grant of Brandaborg, which supposed to be identical to Karlsholm, where he was a courtier in 1457. From between 1457 and 1459 he
2 CONC  was a courtier in Nyköping. Became district chief in Rönö hd in Södermanland between 1455 and 26.1 1458, which he was still 3.6 1462, and lawman in Södermanland 1457 or 1458, which he was still 23.11 1494. Died between 23.11 1494
2 CONC  and 15.8 1495 and was buried in Krokek's monastery. '''Gave 18.1 1445 morning gift to Mechtild Clausdotter, who was still alive 4.5 1460 and was the daughter of Claus Plata in marriage with Cecilia Nilsdotter, whose family's coat
2 CONC  of arms carried the split shield with the left field checkered. On 24 October 1468, Svarte Åke Jönsson gave a morning gift to Birgitta Gregersdotter, who was the daughter of the Riksdag Gregers Matsson ( Lillie ) in marriage to A
2 CONC nna Johansdotter ( Pike ) and died between 1 November 1503 and 12 March 1504 and was buried in Krokek's monastery.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Children:'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * 1. '''Ingeborg Åkedotter.''' Died between 6.2 1477 and 1.2 1480. Received 17.1 1463 gift of morning from the knight and councilor Staffan Bengtsson ( Vinstorpaätten ), who in 1459 became the widower of Birgitta Olofsdotter (Has)
2 CONC  at the latest and fell in the battle of Brunkeberg 10.10 1471. Was 6.2 1477 remarried with the councilor Erik Gustavsson ( Ängaätten ) who died between 12.9 1480 and 7.5 1482.
2 CONT * 1. '''Svarte Jöns Åkeson.''' Supposed to be the "Jhoannes Swarte de Svecia" who in 1467 was promoted to baccalaureus in canon law at the University of Leipzig and then received at the University of Greifswald and in Sept. 1476 w
2 CONC as enrolled at the University of Rostock. Was promoted before 12.2 1479 from canon to archdeacon in Strängnäs. Probably the "Iohannes Swartz de Stregeness" who in 1483 was enrolled at the University of Leipzig. Died as archdeacon 
2 CONC in Strängnäs in 1502. Arfrid Åkedotter. Died no later than 1490 and had then been married to the Riksrader Jöns Knutsson ( Tre rosor ), who in 1477 was the widower of Ingegerd Eriksdotter (Skanke), after Arfrid's death remarried E
2 CONC rmegard Fickedotter ( Bülow ), and died between 1496 and 1498.
2 CONT * 2. '''Mechtild (Brask)''', p. 138). Probably died young.
2 CONT * 2. '''Örjan Åkeson.''' Died young.
2 CONT * 2. '''Axel Åkeson.''' Appears at the earliest on 2.2 1489, died in 1497 or 1498 and was buried in Krokek's monastery.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://www.adelsvapen.com/genealogi/Lillie_af_Greger_Mattssons_%C3%A4tt_nr_6 Adelsvapen Geneologies Lillie of Greger Mattsson's family no. 6]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''TABLE 2'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Greger Mattsson (son of Matts Ödgislesson, Tab. 1), to Tyresö in the same parish, Stockholm county, which he inherited from his grandmother. Was a squire in 1440, knight 1443-06-15 and councilor in 1457. Was King Karl's chieftain 
2 CONC Raseborg As a brother-in-law to Erik Axelsson, he probably assisted in the overthrow of the state in 1457, at least he participated in the decisions that were implemented in the council shortly afterwards, but then King Kristian i
2 CONC n 1463 demanded the opinion of the councilors about Jöns Bengtsson, he participated in all three decisions, which went out on his imprisonment. Sent together with others in 1464 to Danzig to summon King Charles again. Was present 
2 CONC when Jöns Bengtsson was forced to give up his worldly power in the fall of 1466 and was sent s. å. to Raseborg to persuade King Karl to return. After his death in 1470, he stood by Sten Sture's side. Lagman in Västmanland 1478–148
2 CONC 6. Received Stegeborg castle and county 1487-09-03. Lagman in Uppland 1487 until his death. Lived 1494-02-00 21 , but was dead s. å. 22 , when succession was carried out after him 5/11 (according to the tombstone death 1493-03-23)
2 CONC  18 . '''Married 1st to Anna Johansdotter , died approx. 1453, daughter of the knight and councilor Johan Nilsson Gädda and Elin Axelsdotter Brahe .''' Married 2nd shortly after 12/06/1455 to Ramborg Gustafsdotter , died 13/11/149
2 CONC 2. Daughter of the knight and councilor Gustaf Ulfsson Sparre of Hjulsta and Ängsö and Kristina Folkadotter Rossviksätten who carried a Boat in the coat of arms.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Children:'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * 1. '''Brita Gregersdotter ,''' died before 1504-03-12 but after 1503-11-01 when she made a will. Buried in Krokek's monastery/E. '''Married 1468-10-24 (morning gift) to the knight, councilor and lawman in Södermanland Åke Jönsso
2 CONC n ( Svarte Skåning ), to Åkerö, in his 2nd marriage (married 1st 1445-01-18 to Mechtild Clausdotter (Plata), who was still alive in 1460), died in 1494.'''
2 CONT * 1. '''Marina Gregersdotter ,''' was dead in 1459, when she was inherited by her father.
2 CONT * 2. '''Matthias Gregersson .''' Student in Greifswald 1487. Master there. 1490, then doctor decretorum. Enrolled at the University of Cologne 1492-09-07. Kanik in Uppsala. Provost in Strängnäs 1494-11-16. Bishop of Strängnäs 1501
2 CONC -08-27. Riksråd 1502. Was on the side of the Sturars. Bequeathed to Denmark in 1504. Participated in the meetings in Malmö and Copenhagen in 1512 and 1513. Passed after Sten Sture's death in 1520 to King Kristian, but was beheaded
2 CONC . Oh. 8/11 in Stockholm's bloodbath, regardless he and the other councilors agreed to Kristian's acceptance as king, and persuaded the common people to celebrate him and helped at his coronation. (SBL:23 p64 + p67; PhT 1951 p101; 
2 CONC StrHm:1 p373, 455ff; OxoVasa p92f)
2 CONT * 2. '''Bengt Gregersson .''' Knight and Councillor. Died before 1501. to Tyresö and Lagnö. Squire. Riksråd as early as 1485. Knighted in 1497. Held the county of Frösåker as a fief. Lived in 1499. but was dead on 1501-03-12. Marr
2 CONC ied to Märta Arentsdotter , after which inheritance was executed in 1514, daughter of the knight and councilor Arent Bengtsson ( looking back wolf ), to Nynäs, and his 2nd wife Hebbla Albrektsdotter Bydelsbach .
2 CONT * 2. '''Folke Gregersson .''' Knight and Councillor. Died 1507. to Åkerö in Bettna parish, Södermanland county. Was knighted on 16-12-1497, when he received Viste county as a fief. Councilor 1504. Died 1507-04-19. He was accused i
2 CONC n 1497 by vicar Otto in Fröslunda for raping him and eating meat on Fridays. Married 1499-09-15 in Söderköping (morning gift) to Brita Hansdotter , died after 1539-01-16 and before 1541-03-12. Daughter of the knight and lawman in 
2 CONC Närke Hans Åkesson Tott till Bjurum and Frötuna and Kerstin Eriksdotter Gyllenstierna af Lundholm .
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT =History=  
2 CONT
2 CONT .  Uppges 1477 to be 60 years old, although he is mentioned in letters after his brother Ture who was described as 50 years old in 1477. Probably identical to the "Swarte Akow" who was enrolled at the University of Leipzig togethe
2 CONC r with Swedes in 1438. Appears in Sweden no earlier than 1440. Became a knight between 1446 and 19.1. 1449, thus apparently at King Charles's coronation in Uppsala on 29.6. 1448. Was a councillor of the kingdom from at least 1450 
2 CONC and is mentioned as a chieftain at Ringstadaholm on 19.1. 1451 and 1453. In 1454 he received a letter of grant at Brandaborg, which is assumed to be identical to Karlsholm, where he was chieftain in 1457. From between 1457 and 145
2 CONC 9 he was chieftain at Nyköping. Became county sheriff in Rönö hd in Södermanland between 1455 and 26.1 1458, which he was still 3.6 1462, and lawman in Södermanland 1457 or 1458, which he was still 23.11 1494. Died between 23.11 1
2 CONC 494 and 15.8 1495 and was buried in Krokek monastery. Gave 18.1 1445 morning gift to Mechtild Clausdotter, who was still alive 4.5 1460 and was the daughter of Claus Plata in marriage with Cecilia Nilsdotter, whose family in the c
2 CONC oat of arms carried a split shield with the left field checkered. On 24.10.1468, Svarte Åke Jönsson gave a morning gift to Birgitta Gregersdotter, who was the daughter of the councilor Gregers Matsson (Lillie) in marriage with Ann
2 CONC a Johansdotter (Gädda) and died between 1.11.1503 and 12.3.1504 and was buried in Krokek monastery.
2 CONT
2 CONT Owner of Karlsholm, or [http://www.jhbf.se/sid221.html Brandaborg] a fortification at Trindborgen at Brandalsund, Södertälje.
2 CONT * https://www.adelsvapen.com/genealogi/Svarte_Sk%C3%A5ning#TAB_5
2 CONT
2 CONT ==SDHK-nr: [https://sok.riksarkivet.se/?Sokord=karlsholm&EndastDigitaliserat=false&AvanceradSok=False&page=4&postid=sdhk_26863&tab=post#tab 26863]
2 CONT
2 CONT Issued: 14560609, Karlsholm Contents: Magnus Bengtsson and '''Svarte Åke Jönsson''', knights, perform a sibling exchange with their wives' brother Mr. Erik Nipertz, knight at Karlsholm. Present at the exchange were Erengisle Nilss
2 CONC on, Father Ulfsson, Klaus Plata and Canon Birger in Strängnäs. Mr. Erik Nipertz receives two farms in Båresta with the croft Rösarne in Lerbo parish, land in Forssa (Forsaby) in Forssa parish and the croft Jonstorp in Oppunda dist
2 CONC rict, as well as the farm “Wendhebergha” in Skeppsås parish in Boberg district.
2 CONT
2 CONT Erengisle Nilsson, Father Ulfsson, Bo Nilsson and Klaus Plata seal together with the issuers...
2 CONT
2 CONT ==SDHK-nr: [https://sok.riksarkivet.se/?Sokord=s%c3%b6dermanland+lagman++&EndastDigitaliserat=false&AvanceradSok=False&page=159&FacettState=undefined%3ac%7c&postid=sdhk_27182&tab=post#tab 27182]
2 CONT
2 CONT Issued: 14580312, Nyköping Contents: Erik Nipertz, knight, Östgöta lagman, exchanges farms in Väsby and in Ösby in Halla parish in Jönåker district in Strängnäs diocese to '''Mr. Åke Svarte Jönsson, knight, Södermanland lagman''',
2 CONC  for the farm Torlunda in Ripsa parish in Rönö district.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==SDHK-nr: [https://sok.riksarkivet.se/?Sokord=28327&EndastDigitaliserat=false&AvanceradSok=False&page=1&postid=sdhk_28327&tab=post#tab 28327]
2 CONT
2 CONT Issued: 14641028, Vadstena Contents: Knight Svarte Åke Jönsson in Åkerö about eel fishing in Vrena stream in Vrena sn, which he and his siblings inherited from their mother Ingeborg Nilsdotter etc. and siblings Sigge and Bengta.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==SDHK-nr: [https://sok.riksarkivet.se/?Sokord=s%c3%b6dermanland+lagman++&EndastDigitaliserat=false&AvanceradSok=False&page=186&FacettState=undefined%3ac%7c&postid=sdhk_28885&tab=post#tab 28885]
2 CONT
2 CONT Issued: 14681024, Åkerö Contents: Svarte Åke Jönsson, member of parliament and lawman in Södermanland, gives his wife Birgitta Gregersdotter as a gift of land in Harakers and Romfartuna parishes.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==SDHK-nr: [https://sok.riksarkivet.se/?Sokord=s%c3%b6dermanland+lagman++&EndastDigitaliserat=false&AvanceradSok=False&page=202&FacettState=undefined%3ac%7c&postid=sdhk_30673&tab=post#tab 30673]
2 CONT
2 CONT Issued: 14800201, Åkerö Contents: Svarte Åke Jönsson, rd and Södermanland lagman, grants to his son-in-law Erik Gustavsson estates in Vallby in Lunda sn in Jönåkers hd, and in Näs in Ekebyborna sn as well as in Snörbek and Agnesta
2 CONC da in Agne sn in Vartofta hd, which have come to him after his children with Ingeborg Åkesdotter, all now dead.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==SDHK-nr: [https://sok.riksarkivet.se/?Sokord=s%c3%b6dermanland+lagman++&EndastDigitaliserat=false&AvanceradSok=False&page=237&FacettState=undefined%3ac%7c&postid=sdhk_33586&tab=post#tab 33586]
2 CONT
2 CONT Armsman [https://www.geni.com/people/Peter-Ragvaldsson-Fargalt/6000000003645772585  '''Peter Ragvaldsson (Fargalt)'''] in Erstavik, lawman in Södermanland , announces at Hölebo county council in the presence of the well-to-do man 
2 CONC [https://www.geni.com/people/Simon-Ragvaldsson-K%C3%B6rning/4631465 '''Simon (Ragvaldsson) Körning'''] that Anders in Edeby (in Hölö sn) sued Olof in Vreta regarding 2 öresland of land in Väsby (in Trosa- Vagnhärads sn), which acc
2 CONC ording to the plaintiff was pledged to Olof's father. Olof was able to prove that his father Peter Skinnare bought the land from Jöns Smed for 14 marks more than forty years ago when [https://www.geni.com/people/%C3%85ke-J%C3%B6ns
2 CONC son-Svarte-Sk%C3%A5ning/6000000009187591250 '''Mr. (Black) Åke Jönsson'''] owned Karlsholm. Furthermore, the land had lain unobstructed and unelected for so long and was not blamed by Anders until four years ago at the last legisl
2 CONC ative assembly and now at the county council. (...the letter damaged...) Furthermore, Peter and Staffan in Österby confirmed the words of the old Danish man Olof Skäringsson that the land was bought and never mortgaged. On the bas
2 CONC is of these testimonies, the lawman awarded Olof i Vreta the land. The issuer prints his seal on the back of the letter.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==SDHK no: [https://sok.riksarkivet.se/?ValdSortering=DatumStigande&PageSize=50&Sokord=ekebyborna&EndastDigitaliserat=False&AvanceradSok=False&page=29&FacettState=uw8klQ%3Ao&postid=sdhk_30674&tab=post 30674]
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Dating:, 1480 February 2, Place of issue: Åkerö'''
2 CONT
2 CONT The knight Svarte Åke Jönsson in Åkerö makes an agreement on behalf of his granddaughter Mektild Staffansdotter with his 'brother-in-law' (= son-in-law) Erik Gustavsson about silver, gold and chattels in Kavlås and in Vadstena whi
2 CONC ch are Mektild's after his late father Staffan (Bengtsson). Erik is to keep Vallby in Lunda parish, *Näs in Ekebyborna parish as well as Snösbäck and a farm in Agnestad in Agne(stads) parish.
2 CONT
2 CONT Literature and commentary, See DMS, Södermanland 2:3, p. 114. About Mektild Staffansdotter (Vinstorpaätten) see ÄSF I, p. 105. On Erik Gustavsson (Ängaätten) see ÄSF II, p. 118. Cf. SDHK no. 29420 and SDHK no. 30673 .
