1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Gudlög Hansdotter Svinhufvud=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Daughter of Hans Jönsson Svinhufvud and Ingeborg Larsdotter 
2 CONT * The origin of the genus Svinhuvud. Authors: Torsten Berglund, Elisabet Hemström, Leif Olofsson & Anders Winroth. Presentation: »The family has been considered to be descended from a man with the strange name Jöns Swinshow, menti
2 CONC oned in a document from 1386. But after a laboratory examination, history has had to be rewritten somewhat. The genealogists' yearbook 2008.  This doesn’t mean the whole linage is incorrect!
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT =Married=
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT * Married: [https://www.geni.com/photo/view?album_type=photos_of_me&id=6000000001950898729&photo_id=6000000194352930836&position=0 '''Jacob Henriksson Simla'''] who was married to Gudlög Hansdotter (Svinhuvud) daughter of Hans Jön
2 CONC sson (Svinhuvud) and Ingeborg Larsdotter (Korske), the image in Genealogica (o) 26 Image 1290 / page 60 (AID: v914658.b1290.s60 , NAD: SE/RA/7500001).
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://sok.riksarkivet.se/sbl/Presentation.aspx?id=34993&forceOrdinarySite=true Svinhufvud Family, by The Swedish Biographical Lexicon]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Volume 35 (2020-), page 23.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Jöns Swinshwoth (i.e. Svinshuvud) (Berglund et al 2008) bought Höjen and Stämnarvet in Torsångs parish (now Stora Kopparbergs parish) in 1386. He was probably the father of the vicar in Hedemora Dan Jönsson (mentioned 1405–27) and
2 CONC  the miner at Kopparberget Hans Jönsson (mentioned 1434–40), who according to preserved seals both bore the pig's head coat of arms.
2 CONT
2 CONT Hans Jönsson was very likely the father of the miner at Kopparberget Jöns Hansson (mentioned 1450–52) on Höjen. He is mentioned in 1452 as the brother of Gudlög Hansdotter , married to Jakob Henriksson Simla (five-pointed star), f
2 CONC rom whom the noble family Ekeblad (vol. 12) , which became extinct in the 19th century, descended on the paternal side.
2 CONT
2 CONT According to Rasmus Ludvigsson's (bd 29) , the largest family book now only known through old copies (E 8676), the above-mentioned Jöns Hansson was the father of the judge Knut Jönsson (d at the earliest in 1507) at Höjen, who car
2 CONC ried the pig's head coat of arms. His brother (E 8676) Hinse Jönsson (d sometime between 1485–91) at Stämnarvet became the grandfather of the councilors Axel and Knut Anderssöner (Lillie; bd 23) .
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT =Sources=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Gudlög Hansdotter and Jakob Henriksson Simla : Lagergren, a a 1923a, p 179 f; dens, Five nyfunna medeltidsbrev (Dalarna hembygds-förbunds tidskrift, 3, 1923b), p 75; J Raneke, Swedish Medieval Weapons, 2 (1982), p 519; Sweden's 
2 CONC medieval personal names, 2 (1980–91), sp 340.
2 CONT * Sources o litt: General: T Berglund et al, Om släkten Svinhuvud ursborg (Släktforskärnas årsbok 2008), pp. 9–28; T Berglund and A Winroth, Pig's head and horse's head weapons (Vapenbilden 84, 2010), pp. 4–12; B Boëthius, The Kop
2 CONC parbergslagen until the breakthrough of the 1570s (1965); its, Pig's Head and Pig's Ball (PHT 1966, 3–4); S Carlsson, Estate society and estate persons 1700–1865 (1947); Carpelan, 3 (1965); Diplomatarium Dalekarlicum, 1–3 o supple
2 CONC ment (1842–53); The electric trails; H Gillingstam, Svinhuvud och Svinakula (PHT 1966, 1–2); LF Läffler, Some Swedish "talking weapons" (PHT 1903), pp. 77 o 83; BA Nelson, S in Västergötland: some contributions to the genealogy of
2 CONC  the family (SoH 1967); J Raneke, Swedish Medieval Weapons, 1 (1982), p 324, o 3 (1985); SMoK; Supplement to The Introduced Swedish Nobility Genealogies, ed C Szabad (2008); PG Vejde,
2 CONT * Jöns Swinshwoth : Photostat copies of the medieval section, Series II, Booklet no. 16 (after STORA: Grycksbo pappersbruk's archive, vol 11134), RA. Berglund et al, aa; Diplomatarium Dalekarlicum, 1, No. 47; H Lagergren, Släkten 
2 CONC Ekeblad till Stola, 2 (PHT 1923a).
