1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Jacob Henriksson Simla Nr.35=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Son of Häradsdomare Henrik Simla 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://www.adelsvapen.com/genealogi/Ekeblad_nr_35 Oak leaf no. 35 Geneology, by Adelsvapen]
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT *  '''Jakob Henriksson Simla.''' Miner in Karlborn 1440-00-00–1446-00-00. Lived in 1452. 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT =Married=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Married: '''Gudlög Hansdotter,''' daughter of the miner at Stora Kopparberget Hans Jönsson (Svinhuvud).
2 CONT
2 CONT =Children:=
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Hans Jakobsson,''' to Krokfors in Sundborn parish and Sundby manor in Åkers and Ärila parishes, Södermanland county, which he inherited with his wife. Was a member of Stora Kopparberg's district court in 1485 and was named on
2 CONC  1492-03-02 among the twelve dannemen, who were commissioned to carry out inspections regarding the raw passage between Vika and Stora Skedvi parishes. Seems to have moved to Sundby after the last year. Died before 1530. Married (
2 CONC 2:o?) to Brita Andersdotterin her 2nd marriage (married 1st to Erik Pedersson to Dräggesta, who carried a shafted blade in the coat of arms), daughter of the squire and district chief in Österrekarne domsaga Södermanland County, A
2 CONC nders Eriksson (oak blade) and Ingeborg Markvardsdotter Link (1/2 animal). Brita Andersdotter exchanged 1530-03-17 with the consent of the children Anders and Ingeborg to King Gustaf I Sundby manor with subordination to other esta
2 CONC tes [RHKn].
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://sok.riksarkivet.se/sbl/Presentation.aspx?id=34993&forceOrdinarySite=true Svinhufvud Family, by The Swedish Biographical Lexicon]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Volume 35 (2020-), page 23.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Jöns Swinshwoth (i.e. Svinshuvud) (Berglund et al 2008) bought Höjen and Stämnarvet in Torsångs parish (now Stora Kopparbergs parish) in 1386. He was probably the father of the vicar in Hedemora Dan Jönsson (mentioned 1405–27) and
2 CONC  the miner at Kopparberget Hans Jönsson (mentioned 1434–40), who according to preserved seals both bore the pig's head coat of arms.
2 CONT
2 CONT Hans Jönsson was very likely the father of the miner at Kopparberget Jöns Hansson (mentioned 1450–52) on Höjen. '''He is mentioned in 1452 as the brother of Gudlög Hansdotter , married to Jakob Henriksson Simla (five-pointed star)
2 CONC , from whom the noble family Ekeblad (vol. 12) , which became extinct in the 19th century, descended on the paternal side.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT According to Rasmus Ludvigsson's (bd 29) , the largest family book now only known through old copies (E 8676), the above-mentioned Jöns Hansson was the father of the judge Knut Jönsson (d at the earliest in 1507) at Höjen, who car
2 CONC ried the pig's head coat of arms. His brother (E 8676) Hinse Jönsson (d sometime between 1485–91) at Stämnarvet became the grandfather of the councilors Axel and Knut Anderssöner (Lillie; bd 23) .
2 CONT
