1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==Christina Gregorsdotter==
2 CONT
2 CONT * Daughter of the mountain man Gregor Ulfsson (Red Lion) Gammelgården and Margareta Hansdotter (Ekeblad).
2 CONT
2 CONT Måns Knutsson, (son of Knut Knutsson, tab 8), Ribbenäs of Västra Götaland, Värmland County and Blomberg in Husaby Parish, Skaraborg County. Sealed Västerås Inheritance Society 1544-01-13, King Gustaf i's Testament 1560-06-30 and e
2 CONC states bequest 1561. (Hs.) Blomberg was Husaby in the parish of 1558-07-22 and is called Måns Knutsson to Ribbenäs. Lived 1568 and wrote himself yet to Blomberg. (Fs.) Riddarhusgenealogien gives, probably wrongly, that he, who 156
2 CONC 1 and 1568 wrote to Blomberg and then should have been between 70 and 80 years old, is identical to Måns Knutsson to Aspberg in the Victory town Parish, Värmland County, who was tiondefogde in Värmland 1561 – 1567 and bailiff in Ö
2 CONC stersysslet 1562 – 1570 (Al.), in the Castle holidays at Läckö 1567-02-10, bailiff at Örebro Castle 1571 – 1578 (Al.) and who lived even 1581 (Al.), and which was son in law to Botvid Larsson Anckar. Married (1: o) with Christina 
2 CONC Gregorsdotter, daughter of the mountain man Gregor Ulfsson (Red Lion) Gammelgården and Margareta Hansdotter (Ekeblad). ? Married 2: O 1569 with Margareta Botvidsdotter, daughter of the commanding officer Botvid Larsson (Anckar, nr
2 CONC  108) and Karin Svensdotter's daughter Kart.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Children:==
2 CONT
2 CONT * 1. Axel Månsson. Lived without service. See Tab. 88.
2 CONT * 1. Ingrid Månsdotter. Married to captain at the Uppland flag (BLR.) Joen Andersson, ennobled Torskenstierna, but not introduced, to Hallsta in Björksta Parish, Västmanland county, probably dead 1569. (BLR.)
2 CONT * 1. Bengta Månsdotter. Married to the Foundation man and war Colonel Peder Nilsson, ennobled Gyllenstråle (No. 256), who lived 1587.
2 CONT * 1. Anders Månsson, dead Young.
2 CONT * 1. Ingel Månsson, dead Young.
2 CONT * 1. Gregory Månsson, dead Young.
2 CONT * 1. Margareta Månsdotter, dead Young.
2 CONT * 1. Brita Månsdotter, died 1614-07-24 and buried in Falu Church. Married 1: O With Daniel Tor Kil's son (ennobled Svinhufvud), who lived 1581, in his 2nd marriage. Married 2: O After 1595, but before (SK.) 1601-01-20 with the Ric
2 CONC h mountain man Christoffer Olsson, ennobled Gyllenknoster 1621-01-30, but not introduced, in Nor, in his 2nd married.
2 CONT * 1. Bryngel Månsson. Bailiff at Västerås Castle 1597 (1597-02-09) – 1602 (Al.). Had according to royal letter 1594-05-04 in fief a church homestead in St. Ilians Parish, Västmanland County, which he himself used to 1599. (Al.)
2 CONT * 1. Anders Månsson, dead Young.
