2 CONT Content
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://www.geni.com/photo/view/6000000008258771909?album_type=photos_of_me&photo_id=6000000191614703901 '''Archbishop Birger(Gregersson) in Uppsala'''] attributes (Confessor General Peter Olofsson in Vadstena Kloster) and thanks
2 CONC  for a sent legend about the Holy Virgin and asks the recipient of the letter to send the entire office about the Holy Virgin at the appropriate time. Furthermore, thanks for a recently sent letter, which mentions a revelation tha
2 CONC t the late wife Birgitta (Birgersdotter) had regarding this officium. Regarding the writing of the rhyming office ("composicionem hystorie") about Mrs. Birgitta, which the issuer has already sent to the recipient, except for the m
2 CONC ass office that is now being transmitted - with the exception of the sequence that was sent around Passion Sunday with Arvid Djäken - the archbishop does not want his own acumen to be attributed the merit of this, but praises the 
2 CONC Lord who has given his help thanks to the intercession of the Virgin Mary and wife Birgitta. Furthermore, the issuer points out that he found two errors in the rhyme scheme sent to the recipient of the letter. One error is found i
2 CONC n the prologue (that is, the first reading) and the other at the end of the ninth reading, where the day of (Birgitta's) translation to Vadstena monastery is mentioned. According to Mr. Karl, this did not take place on August 1 bu
2 CONC t in the month of July; the recipient of the letter is requested to correct this personally and to inform the issuer of the translation date, so that he can correct his own additions. In addition, the archbishop sends back a bundl
2 CONC e containing miracles, sealed with the seal of the issuer and provided with a notary mark. The recipient of the letter is asked to send the rhyme office together with the mass office to the bishop (Tomas Johansson) in Växjö, so th
2 CONC at he, who is the issuer's 'teacher and master', will correct what needs to be corrected. Furthermore, the recipient and Mr. Birger (Ulfsson) are asked to recommend the issuer to Mr. Alfonso, former bishop of Jaén, when they write
2 CONC  to him. The archbishop says he is ready to readily obey his exhortations. Finally, the recipient of the letter is asked to have faith in the words that the mailman Karl, on behalf of the issuer, communicates to the recipient and 
2 CONC Mr. Birger (Ulfsson). Furthermore, the recipient and Mr. Birger (Ulfsson) are asked to recommend the issuer to Mr. Alfonso, former bishop of Jaén, when they write to him. The archbishop says he is ready to readily obey his exhorta
2 CONC tions. Finally, the recipient of the letter is asked to have faith in the words that the mailman Karl, on behalf of the issuer, communicates to the recipient and Mr. Birger (Ulfsson). Furthermore, the recipient and Mr. Birger (Ulf
2 CONC sson) are asked to recommend the issuer to Mr. Alfonso, former bishop of Jaén, when they write to him. The archbishop says he is ready to readily obey his exhortations. Finally, the recipient of the letter is asked to have faith i
2 CONC n the words that the mailman Karl, on behalf of the issuer, communicates to the recipient and Mr. Birger (Ulfsson).
2 CONT
2 CONT The issuer seals with his secret.
2 CONT
2 CONT
