2 CONT
2 CONT The Swedish Diplomatarium's main index of medieval letters
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Dating: 1366 July 6, Place of issue: Skipper City ''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT Peter Virdske announces that he has sold all his property in Långö to '''Ragnvald Erengislesson (Puke)''' and legally assigned it to him and his heirs for perpetual possession.
2 CONT
2 CONT The issuer and Abbot Sven of Nydala, Mr. Bonde, provost of the Western District, seal.
2 CONT
2 CONT * Sources: Original:  Or. perg., RA 0101  images,Medieval copies:  A 134 a, page 23, KB,Post-medieval copies:  Brocman: II Misc. 18:34
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Letter text'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Alla them(a) mæn thætta bref høra ælla se helsa iak pætar wridzke(b) mæÞ guthi æwærdlilika (c ) * thætta skal allum mannum kunnukth wara mik haua saalt hætherlikum oc skællikum manne ' ragnelde(d) æringislasyni(e) alt mit goz i la
2 CONC ngethe(f) mæÞ allo thy ther til liggir j akrum ok ' j ænghium(g) fiskwætnum oc qwærn mæÞ wato oc thorro before garz oc vtan / ængho vtan(h) ' takno / hanum oc hans aruum iak lagfæst thet / vndan mik oc minum aruum til æwærdlilika(
2 CONC j) ' æghø (k ) * scriptum et actum skiparstathum(l) anno domini M ccc lx sexto in octaua sanctorum apostolorum petri et pauli V Jn cuius rei testimonium sigilis virorum honorabilium videlicet venerabilis patris domini swenonis abb
2 CONC atis ' novevallis(m) et domini bondonis prepositj in wæstra hæreth(n) vna cum proprio(o) feci presentes consignarj
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Extra text'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * On the back: hedisryd næssia et sundreda commutata in langedeWith a slightly later style: langedhe
2 CONT SEAL: Of the 3 seals, no. 1 is missing, but the strip of which remains. No. 2 and 3 are fragmentary. No. 2, pointed oval, shows a standing man with his right hand raised. The circumscription reads: ... .OVEVALLIS. No. 3, round, wi
2 CONC th circumscription: .....NIS:PBR'. Brocman states, not entirely correctly, that only no. 2 is attached. Of its circumscription he notes: "S. abb. novevallis". For no. 2 see now Kyrkohist. årsskr. 1965, pp. 89, 102.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://sok.riksarkivet.se/?Sokord=Ragvald+Erengislesson+Puke&EndastDigitaliserat=true&AvanceradSok=False&page=1&postid=sdhk_5222&tab=post SDHK no: 5222]
2 CONT The Swedish Diplomatarium's main catalog of medieval letters
2 CONT * '''Dating: 1345 September 14, Place of issue "Median Isthmus"
2 CONT
2 CONT Erengisle Petersson explains that his brother-in-law Nils Uddsson left an account of everything, both loose and fixed, that he took care of. Witnesses present at the accounting were Bengt Puke, Petrus Asmundson, Tyrgils de Asyndum
2 CONC , Mr. Botolf de Helgerulte, Peter Erengisleson, '''Ragvald Erengisleson''' Bengt Puke, Peter Jordason, Rörik Tureson, Peter Asmundsson, Peter Erengisleson, Ragvald Erengisleson and the issuer seal.
2 CONT
2 CONT Latin: Källor Eftermedeltida avskrifter: B 15, fol. 34v, RA 0202
2 CONT
2 CONT To all who see the present writing, I, Eringislo Pætharsson, greet you in the Lord forever. I want it to be clearly evident to everyone, both posterity and moderns, that I have received a full account of everything that passed bet
2 CONC ween my beloved husband and my beloved son-in-law Nicolaus Vdsson, and myself be considered by name, either for movables or for immovables. Now that I am satisfied, and I go away grateful [d.v.s.: from him], and I return to him gr
2 CONC ateful [d.v.s.: thanks] for the gracious conversation [d.v.s.: thanks] I will give myself (?) in many forms (?), and [d.v.s.: vt] I leave the above-mentioned free and [d.v.s.: vt] left, because the discreet men - - - - had been pr
2 CONC esent the aforesaid, that is to say, Benedict Puka, Peter Asmundason, Lord Thirchillus of Asydum, and Lord Botolphus of Hæalgerultæ, and Peter of Eringislon, and Raguald of Eringislon. for greater evidence I ask for the seals of t
2 CONC he discreet men Benedict Puka, Petri Jordason, and Røryci Twrason, Petri Asmundason, Petri Eringislonis, and Raguald Eringislonis, with my seal here affixed, Written and acted in my Median court, on [the day] of the Exaltation of 
2 CONC the Holy Cross in the Year of the Lord M. 300 40 fifth
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://sok.riksarkivet.se/dokument/sdhk/5222.pdf Seal]
2 CONT
2 CONT Enligt ritningen hafva de six första sigillen varit borta; blott No. 7, Ragvald Eringislesons (båt) is drawn. Trykt DS 3993 se pdf av tryk Litteratur och kommentar See SDHK nr 5947 (DS 4554)
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://sok.riksarkivet.se/?Sokord=Ragvald+Erengislesson+Puke&EndastDigitaliserat=true&AvanceradSok=False&page=1&postid=sdhk_5947&tab=post#tab SDHK no: 5947]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''The Swedish Diplomatarium's main catalog of medieval letters'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Dating: 1350 March 30'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Peter, Rangvald (Puke)''' and Filip Eringislesöner and Nils Udsson, with the consent of their father Eringisle Petersson and their mother Bengta, their fathers and mothers in 4 brother lots, because they gave their sister Ingeb
2 CONC org full and equal brother lots with themselves, whereby Peter Bonde gets Ullavi (Norrvidinge district) and Rottne (Söraby parish, Norrvidinge district) etc., Rangvald Puke sheep estate in Västra härad in Njudung, Filip Eringisles
2 CONC on sheep Kianäs (Älghult parish, Uppvidinge härad) etc. and Ingeborg gets Källeflaga (Åseda parish, Uppvidinge county) etc. 
2 CONT
2 CONT * Erengisle Petersson, wife Bengta, Peter Bonde, Rangvald Puke, Filip and Niklas Udsson, Rörik Bonde, Peter Bonde, Johannes Brudson seal
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Letter Text'''
2 CONT
2 CONT To all the men who hear and see this letter, we Peter Æringgislasson and Ranguualdar Æringgislasson and Philipus Æringgislasson and Niklas Wdsson, with whom the lord and William are acquainted, that it may be known to all men, who
2 CONC  are now and who shall come, that we have made a division of the matter, that the fathers and mothers were with our father Æringgislla Petersson, the good woman, and the mother of his wife Bendicto, and the wife and relatives of t
2 CONC he king, that we have divided the fathers and mothers into four brotherhoods, for that we have given our sister Inggeborghe Æringisladotur full brotherhood and equal with us. This is the first brother's lot, Wllaui and Røtne with 
2 CONC another Kuernnastrøm and two other lands, and Løppanæs with another land and Karlsþorp, and this is our will, that our son Pætar Bondde get this same lot; and another brother's lot is all that lies in the Western region in Niuþung
2 CONC ge, and that we want, that our son Rangualdar Puke has; and the third brother's lot is Kidiænæs with a village called Kimbbara malle, and all the ægholat in Houlitta waþa and warn ægholat in Allem with all that lies there, and tha
2 CONC t we want that our son Philippus has; and the four brothers Keldoflagha with all that was buried there in the year and Nyanæs and Myrtleka kwern and Myklahult and the wild land we, that was daughter Inggeborgh had, and with their 
2 CONC excuses, that the land, which is not well-known for these, lies Asmoþaboþahult to the jamkan fört. Then all the reason why the wine and why the relatives seem to be equal was discussed and then you said that, as he wanted, he woul
2 CONC d bring forth forty marks to the others, who did not want to come, and to this that this is his great status, the seats we here fore were sealed, as Æringgisl Pætarsson and my dear wife Benedicta and Pætar Bondde and Rangualdar Pu
2 CONC ke and Philippus and Niklas Wdsson and bethus here fore with what seals heþarlika menna and erlika insigle, my dear brothers Mr. Røriks Bondda and Pætars Bondda and Johannes Bruzson, and this was given by the Lord byrdh þussanda a
2 CONC rum þþy hundraþa arum þy fiftighi arum a þþia dagh paska.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://sok.riksarkivet.se/dokument/sdhk/5947.pdf '''Seal''']
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://sok.riksarkivet.se/?Sokord=Ragvald+Erengislesson+Puke&EndastDigitaliserat=false&AvanceradSok=False&page=2&postid=sdhk_9696&tab=post SDHK-nr: 9696]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''The Swedish Diplomatarium's main catalog of medieval letters'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Date: 1370 May 18, Place of issue: Rörvik.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Johan Tyrgilsson sells to '''Ragvald Erengislesson (Puke)''' and his heirs his entire ancestral inheritance in Ånhult (in Sandsjö parish) for 80 marks of good money and acknowledges that, even if the estate were worth more, he has
2 CONC  received full consideration for this. If the estate is taken from Ragvald Erengislesson, Johan Tyrgilsson undertakes to hold him and his heirs harmless. 
2 CONT * The letter issuer seals together with the knight Mr. Johan Hjärne, the abbot Mr. Sven (in Nydala monastery), Magnus Uddolfsson and Peter Virske.
2 CONT
2 CONT * Sources: Medieval copies: Copy in vidimation on perg. 1424 17/10, SDHK no. 20357, Sv. Riksarkivet. Post medieval copies: Brocman: Misc. 74:21, Regesta norvegica: 1370-1390 Nr: 946 Dato:	1381 mai 13 Sted:	Alleby på Hisingen
2 CONT
2 CONT =Speculative hunch, but a reasonable hypothesis.=
2 CONT
2 CONT Hi Roger,
2 CONT
2 CONT I think I have identified the family affiliation of Gjurd Karlsson's wife, Elin Ragvaldsdotter! Enough 'boundary conditions' are met to claim this. My hypothesis is that Elin was a daughter of Ragvald Erengisle Puke, son of Erengi
2 CONC sle Petersson Bonde o.h.h. Bengta Ragvaldsdotter Puke.
2 CONT
2 CONT The first argument is of course the name Erengisle – Elin's son was named after her grandfather.
2 CONT
2 CONT The second argument is land tenure. Gjurd's wife had her own holdings in Linderås and Frinnaryd, as did her first husband, Bengt Magnusson's, probable aunt Bengta Nilsdotter [J Raneke, p. 200]. In the same area, several members of
2 CONC  the relevant Bonde family own estates for several generations.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''As an example, it can be mentioned that Elin's postulated cousin (after Erengisle Petersson Bonde), Filip Bonde bought "Blaesatorp" in Linderås in 1425 [SDHK 20471]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Furthermore, in 1524 the squire Thord Bonde gave Vadstena Kloster his estate and his farm in Linderås church village.
2 CONT
2 CONT The most important arguments are, after all, in documents potentially documented family relationships:
2 CONT
2 CONT '''SDHK 7043, 1356-07-21 Contents:''' Bengta Nilsdotter in Hästeryd sells to Peter Bonde half an eighth of land in Frinnaryd for 30 marks penningar. Torsten Simonsson, Nils Upplänning, Peter Ragvaldsson and the issuer seal.
2 CONT
2 CONT According to above, Bengta was probably an aunt of Bengt Magnusson, and Peter (Erengisle) Bonde was Elin Ragvaldsdotter's uncle. The letter is sealed by, among others, Peter Ragvaldsson - probably Elin's brother. Elin.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''SDHK-nr: 7042, 1356-07-21''' Bredestad (Norra Vedbo) Contents: The Lord Mayor of Vedbo Peter Rangvaldsson, announces land sold by Bengta Nilsdotter to Peter Bonde in Frinnaryd. Parish priest Erik i Marbek seals.
2 CONT
2 CONT Among the fasts is a Bengt Magnusson - possibly / likely Elin's future husband?
2 CONT
2 CONT '''SDHK no: 14847, 1397-08-08'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Bulsjö
2 CONT
2 CONT Content: Nils Uddsson and Pelle Germundsson trade the district chief in Ydre Gjurd Fot a farm in "Graffby" for his homestead in Norra Höglycke.
2 CONT
2 CONT Nils Uddsson's wife was Ingeborg Erengisledotter (Farmer) - an aunt of Elin!
2 CONT
2 CONT However, a hypothesis is not worth much if it does not have a high explanatory value.
2 CONT Göran Sparrlöf writes on p. 231 about Gjurd's wife Elin Ragvaldsdotter: "She may have been a significant landowner at the local level and it looks as if she was related to earl Erengisle Sunesson."
2 CONT
2 CONT According to the hypothesis, they were cousins ​​after the knight Ragvald Puke and Katarina Karlsdotter (lion beam)!
2 CONT
2 CONT Sparrlöf further writes (p. 226) "Of particular interest is the morning gift letter, which the knight Harald Karlsson (Stubbe) issued from his seat farm Åhlult in Södra Vi parish, Sevede härad, 1398 11/6. In this, Gjurd Fot is lis
2 CONC ted among the fasts (SRP no. 2917). Harald Karlsson had a family relationship with earl Erengisle Sunesson (boat), which apparently Elin Ragvaldsdotter also had."
2 CONT
2 CONT According to the hypothesis, Harald Karlsson's father, Karl Haraldsson, was the cousin of earl Erengisle Sunesson (boat) - Elin's cousin
2 CONT
