2 CONT = Tord Bonde, by Wikipedia=
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Tord Bonde From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia Jump to: navigation, search Lord Tord Röriksson, nicknamed Bonde, Lord of Penningby (born in 1350s, died 21 March 1417, Toordh Bonde in his era's Eastern Norse language; Tord Bonde 
2 CONC in today Swedish) was a medieval Swedish magnate.
2 CONT
2 CONT Tord Bonde was born into the highest nobility of his era's Sweden. His parents were lord Rörik Tordsson (of the Bonde) and lady Märta Gisladotter (of the so-called Sparre of Aspnäs). Tord Bonde was married to lady Ramborg Nilsdott
2 CONC er (of the Vasa family).
2 CONT
2 CONT Quite young, he was entrusted with the position of castellan of Raseborg, Finland. He was knighted and appointed a Royal Councillor. Later, he allied himself with Queen Margaret I of Denmark and benefited from being her trusted ag
2 CONC ent. In 1403 lord Tord received an appointment as chatelain of Viipuri castle and county, at which office he would serve until his death.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1404, he started to launch offensives against Russians that led to a new treaty. In September 1408, hostilities opened again. Tord Bonde fought the Russians by, for example, using sea piracy against their commerce. In 1409 agai
2 CONC n a new treaty brought further advantages to the Swedish. Around 1411 Russians, having felt Viipuri a haven of hostile actions and aggression, launched an attack. Most of the town was destroyed. However, the castle did not surrend
2 CONC er, the besiegers ultimately retreated, and peace was restored.
2 CONT
2 CONT His son Knut Bonde died in 1413, a couple of years after having had a son of his own, Charles Knutsson (1408-70), who would become King of Sweden in 1448. Tord's second son was Karl Bonde, and Tord's daughter Margareta Tordsdotter
2 CONC  married lord Ivar Nilson. His other grandchildren included Tord Carlsson Bonde the marshal, and lady Ingeborg Ivarsdotter, who would become mother of five of the Tott Axelssons.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
