1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Ingeborg Magnusdotter oä Folkunge=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Daughter of Magnus Birgersson and Ingegerd Filipsdotter
2 CONT * '''Ingeborg Magnusdotter.''' Lived in 1331, brought in the estate goods in Åkers hd in Södermanland. Still alive in 1358, when she and the children passed on the inheritance to the husband. — Married on 4 October 1324 in Stockho
2 CONC lm to Karl Dansson (Stjärnbjälke), who is mentioned in 1319, was still alive on 21 October 1354 but died on 6 May 1358.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://www.geni.com/photo/view?album_type=photos_of_me&id=6000000003791053983&photo_id=6000000225648232888&position=0 Children based on Summary Table of Verified Medieval Documents (SHK/ DS)]
2 CONT {{https://www.geni.com/media/proxy?media_id= 6000000225648232888&&size=large}}  
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT =Children=  
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Ingegärd Karlsdotter Stjärnbalk;''' SDHK-nr: 7289 (1358): Ingegärd is explicitly named alongside her sister Ingrid and mother Ingeborg in the inheritance split (arvskifte) following her father’s death. SDHK-nr: 5837 & 7289: T
2 CONC hese primary sources prove she was married to Ragvald Nilsson (Fargalt), whom her father Karl Dansson explicitly calls his måg (son-in-law) as early as 1354. Through this marriage, the Fargalt family inherited the prominent Hedens
2 CONC ö estate. SDHK-nr: 11853 (1381): She and her husband remained active in defending their inherited Södermanland properties in a major royal court case decades later.Genealogical
2 CONT * '''Per Karlsson Stiernbielke;''' He is listed in SDHK number: 7289 as an heir of inheritance in the  Swedish Diplomatarium's main index of medieval letters.
2 CONT * '''Ingrid Karlsdotter Stiernbielke;''' She is listed as a daughter in SDHK number: 7289. She was married to  Bengt Larsson bjälke från Västergötland based on SDHK-nr: 11853 (1381): A royal court judgment tracks a long-standing p
2 CONC roperty dispute over lands that Karl Dansson and his wife mortgaged to their son-in-law Bengt Larsson. Because the mortgage took place during Karl Dansson's lifetime (prior to 1358), and because Ingrid's sister Ingegärd was marrie
2 CONC d to Ragvald Nilsson, by a clear process of elimination, Ingrid's husband is proven to be Bengt Larsson.
2 CONT * '''Daan  Karlsson Stiernbielke;''' He is listed in SDHK number: 7289 as an heir of inheritance in the  Swedish Diplomatarium's main index of medieval letters.
2 CONT * '''NN Karlsdotter (Stjärnbjälke);''' Based on SDHK-nr: 7288, Date: 1358, Regarding information about a letter in which Mrs. Ingeborg Magnusdotter makes an exchange with her son-in-law Ragvald Erengislesson Puke. This is proof a 
2 CONC daughter was married to Ragvald Erengislesson Puke in 1358, who was a 14th-century Swedish esquire (väpnare) belonging to the prominent noble Bonde family. He lived during a turbulent political era in medieval Scandinavia, appeari
2 CONC ng in historical records between 1345 and 1381, and passed away before March 1393 (likely between 1381 and 1384). He is notable for adopting the surname Puke from his maternal lineage, creating a distinct branch within the noble B
2 CONC onde clan.  
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://sok.riksarkivet.se/?Sokord=Ragvald+Erengislesson+Puke&EndastDigitaliserat=false&AvanceradSok=False&page=1&postid=sdhk_7288&tab=post SDHK-nr: 7288]
2 CONT
