2 CONT ==[http://www.adelsvapen.com/genealogi/Folkunga%C3%A4ttens_o%C3%A4kta_gren#TAB_3 Folkungaättens oäkta gren]
2 CONT
2 CONT Magnus Gregersson (son of Gregers, tab. 1). Mentioned on 19.10 1285. Was a squire in 1286 and a knight in 1288. Belonged to King Birger's council apparently already in 1291 and in any case in 1299. Was a lawman in Västmanland in 1
2 CONC 305. Mentioned as alive no later than 13.12 1319. Was dead on 9.1 1326 and was buried with the Dominicans in Sigtuna. Had paternal estate on Arnö in övergrans sn in Håbo hd in Uppland, which he sold to Uppsala cathedral. Owned Bru
2 CONC nnsholm in Näs sn in Åsunda hd in Uppland as well as several landed properties on Ängsö in the same mentioned sn in Yttertjurbo hd in Västmanland, which he exchanged for land in Vallentuna hd in Uppland. In addition, he owned stra
2 CONC w goods in Rasbo, Hagunda, Ulleråkers and Vaksala hd in Uppland. '''Married the first time after 27.9 1282 but before 10.12 1288 to Ragnhild Erlandsdotter who was the daughter of Mr. Erland Israelsson (Finstaätten) and Katarina Jo
2 CONC hansdotter (Ängel), and who had previously been married to Mr. Johan Karlsson (Fånöätten), executed in 1280.''' She drew up her will 10.12 1288 and then chose his camp town at the preacher brothers in Sigtuna. '''Magnus Gregersson
2 CONC  was then, before 4.11 1295, remarried to Ingegärd Filipsdotter, daughter of the knight Filip Finvidsson (Rumbyätten) and a daughter of Karl Tjelvason (Fånöätten).''' As a widow, Ingegärd made her will in 1326 and chose her camp t
2 CONC own with the preacher brothers in Sigtuna. Still alive 16.2 1328.
2 CONT
2 CONT =Children=
2 CONT
2 CONT * 1. '''Peter Magnusson.''' Was underage in 1298 and again in 1302. Was dead on 3.12 1310, when he was buried and his father made his will, in which legacies were assigned to the churches in Fittja in Lagunda hd in Uppland and in 
2 CONC Aspö in Selebo hd in Södermanland, where he apparently owned property. The farm Dalby in Aspö sn in Selebo hd was also determined as a pledge for the legacy. Owned mother land in Frötuna shipyard in Uppland. Inherited from his mat
2 CONC ernal uncle, the canine Karl Erlandsson, land in Färentuna hd in Uppland. Surrendered in 1310 to Sko Kloster for atonement for committed violence land in Frösåkers and Färentuna hd in Uppland, as well as in Svartlösa and Hölebo hd
2 CONC  in Södermanland. Was married to Helena, who was called domina but did not have her own seal.
2 CONT * 2. '''Gregers Magnusson,''' 1318, died trol. 1348, knight, councillor, drots. See tab. 4.
2 CONT * 2. '''Ingeborg Magnusdotter.''' Lived in 1331, brought in the estate goods in Åkers hd in Södermanland. Still alive in 1358, when she and the children passed on the inheritance to the husband. — Married on 4 October 1324 in Stoc
2 CONC kholm to Karl Dansson (Stjärnbjälke), who is mentioned in 1319, was still alive on 21 October 1354 but died on 6 May 1358.
2 CONT * 2. '''Margareta Magnusdotter.''' Entered Sko Cistercian monastery before 1318. Still alive 29.5 1328.
2 CONT * 2. '''Kristina Magnusdotter.''' Called "domina Cristina, neptis mea", in her maternal uncle Jedvard Filipsson's will in 1328. Lived in 1361 in Stockby on Lidingön. On 21.9 1364 she entered St. Klara monastery in Stockholm with l
2 CONC and in Skepptuna sn in Seminghundra hd in Uppland. Was before 25.3 1327 and probably also before 22.10 1324 married to the Riksdag knight Finvid Nilsson (Frössviksätten), who appears in the records no earlier than 5.6 1298 and, we
2 CONC ak in body, made his will 25.3 1327, when he chose his camp town in Skokloster.
2 CONT * 2. '''Knut Magnusson.''' Mentioned 1326-1328 as preacher brother in Sigtuna.
2 CONT * 2. '''Karl Magnusson,''' 1328—1347. See tab. 6.
2 CONT * 2. '''Johan Magnusson,''' 1328—1340, knight, lawman (? subordinate). See tab. 11.
2 CONT * 2. '''Helena Magnusdotter.''' Died no later than 1345. Married no later than 1318 to Riksrad Karl Orestason (Färla, Oreste Keldorsson's family), who is mentioned in 1312 and was still alive in 1335 but was dead in 1345.
2 CONT
2 CONT
