1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT =Agda "Caritas" Persdotter=
2 CONT
2 CONT * AGDA PERSDOTTER or Agda i Porten, (d. after 1565), was a Swedish woman, main royal mistress of King Eric XIV of Sweden during his time as a Crown Prince and during the first years of his reign 1560-1565.
2 CONT
2 CONT =Biography=
2 CONT
2 CONT Agda Persdotter is believed to have been the daughter of the wealthy merchant Peder Klementsson, who lived by St Nicolai port in Stockholm and was known as Per i porten, though her parentage has not been confirmed. She was describ
2 CONC ed as a very beautiful woman and was called Caritas. She became the mistress of Eric during his time as a crown prince and is the first of his recorded mistresses, was a center of his court at Kalmar Castle 1558, where a chamber, 
2 CONC "Agdas kammare", ("Agda's chamber") is still named after her, and their relationship continued after he became king in 1560. https://www.kalmarslott.se/utstaellningar/agdakammaren
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1561, she was married to the nobleman Joakim Fleming and given the estate Eknaholm outside Växjö, which had belonged to a monastery, and the relationship ended and continued after she became a widow in 1563. The relationship wa
2 CONC s not exclusive, as Eric had a large number of other mistresses; the period 1561-65, Anna Larsdotter, Karin Jacobsdotter, Karin Pedersdotter, Sigrid Nilsdotter, Doredi Valentinsdotter and the more anonymous Britta and Ingrid was a
2 CONC ll listed as the King's mistresses, but Agda was his main mistress. The position of these women was only half official.
2 CONT
2 CONT She had several daughters with Eric and one daughter with Joakim Fleming, Anna, (born 1562). In 1561, the custody of her children was given to the king's sister, Princess Cecilia of Sweden, because: "I know she is not capable of r
2 CONC aising them in good discipline and other things". When Cecilia left the country in 1564, the care, as well as the care of the other children of Eric, was given to Princess Elizabeth of Sweden; one of Elizabeth's servants, Karin Må
2 CONC nsdotter, took care of Virginia. In 1565, Karin became the one and only mistress of Eric and replaced both Agda and all the others. Agda remarried Christoffer Olsson Stråle av Sjöared, sheriff of Stegeborg.
2 CONT
2 CONT =Children with King Eric XIV of Sweden=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Virginia Eriksdotter (1559–1633) (living descendants)
2 CONT * Constantia Eriksdotter (1560–1649) (living descendants)
2 CONT * Lucretia Eriksdotter (1564–after 1574) died young.
2 CONT
2 CONT =History of Agda Persdotter=
2 CONT
2 CONT Agda Persdotter, also known as "Agda in the gate", with unknown birth and death, was the Mistress of the same name in 1558 – 61 and possibly 1563 – 65.
2 CONT
2 CONT Her year of birth is unknown. Agda has been declared the daughter of the magistrate Peder Klemetsson in St. Nicolai Port in Stockholm, a task which, however, has so far been impossible to verify. The father, however, has been a al
2 CONC derman and wealthy merchant in Stockholm, originating in Finland. Agda was called "Caritas" (Latin: Affection, Love) for the sake of her beauty.
2 CONT
2 CONT Agda Persdotter was Erik's first mistress. It is unknown when they began their relations, but it was probably begun in Stockholm. She is confirmed as crown Prince Erik's mistress after his move to Kalmar 1558, where she got her ow
2 CONC n room in his residence called "Agdas chamber". The room was next to Erik's reception room. That the relationship started already in Stockholm is illustrated by the fact that the couple's daughter Virginia was born on 1 January 15
2 CONC 59, seven months after Agda arrived in Kalmar in May 1558. Erik should not have had any other mistress during this time.
2 CONT
2 CONT Agda Persdotter had at least two daughters with Erik XIV, Virginia and Constantia:
2 CONT
2 CONT * Virginia Eriksdotter (1559 – 1633), married to governor Håkan Knutsson (Hand) .
2 CONT * Constantia Eriksdotter (1560 – 1649), married to Häradshövdingen Henrik Franke Lin (d. 1610), known for his long journeys in Eastern Europe.
2 CONT * Lucretia (born 1564), has been deposed as the daughter of Agda, but there is no evidence of this. Lucretia is reported in a source to have been married to a Daniel Zelow.  Erik himself set up a horoscope of both Virginia and Con
2 CONC stantia. A third illegitimate daughter of Erik XIV, 
2 CONT
2 CONT In the autumn of 1560 Erik planned a trip to England to be free to Queen Elizabeth, and thus he was expected to do away with his mistress, as was the custom when a prince entered into marriage. He brought Agda to Stockholm, where 
2 CONC she begat the couple's second daughter, Constantia, on June 13. On 25 August 1560 was conferred Agda Eknaholms Gård, which is regarded as her pension. In September, however, Erik was king and his trip to England had to be canceled
2 CONC . It is unknown whether Agda remained as Erik's mistress during this time, but it is believed to be probable. In September 1561, Erik planned to resume the trip to England. The trip was cancelled again, but Agda still ceased to be
2 CONC  Erik's mistress.
2 CONT
2 CONT On September 24, 1561, Erik ceded custody of his daughters with Agda to his sister Cecilia. He also gives Cecilia permission to use force and all the means she considers necessary to take over the children from Agda. Agda married 
2 CONC in September 1561 with Erik's Chamberlain, nobleman Joakim Eriksson Fleming (1534 – 1563), brother of the Finnish hövitsman Clas Eriksson Fleming. The marriage had been arranged before Erik's trip to England, with the idea that it
2 CONC  was necessary if Erik entered into marriage, but got off even though the trip was cancelled. At the wedding, she received in addition to the previously appointed Eknamholm in Småland also several tax-free properties in Södermanla
2 CONC nd. With Fleming, Agda had the daughter Anna (born 1562).
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1563 she became a widow, and it is possible that she was then mistress to Erik again. In 1565, all Erik's favourites were replaced by Karin Månsdotter. Agda Persdotter's further life is unknown, but there is information that sh
2 CONC e should have married Christoffer Olofsson Ray of Lakes, Royal Commanders and Commandant at stegeborg Castle and Söderköping Castle. Her death is unknown.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Source''' - https://sv.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Agda_Persdotter
2 CONT
2 CONT =Links=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Wikipedia  - https://sv.wikipedia.org/wiki/Agda_Persdotter
2 CONT * Agda Persdotter Lover to Erik XIV.http://historiska-personer.nu/min-s/pbc120aa0.html
2 CONT * Gustafsson-Vasa, Erik XIV »- http://www.igen.se/farmor/index.htm?/farmor/010/00/066.htm
2 CONT * Runeberg - http://runeberg.org/sqvinnor/0012.html  
2 CONT
2 CONT =Sources=
2 CONT
2 CONT Hans Gillingstam, "Agda Persdotter, hennes släkt och Erik XIV:s dotter Lucretia. En källkritisk studie", Släkt och Hävd 2001:2-3, s. 156-160. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Herman Lindqvist, "Historien om Sverige: Gustav Vasa och hans söner och döttrar." 
2 CONT
2 CONT Lars-Olof Larsson, "Arvet efter Gustav Vasa" 
2 CONT
2 CONT Frillohopen - https://sv.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Frillohopen
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Agda En utmärkt vacker borgarflicka, som på sin tid gjorde mycket buller, eller snarare gaf
2 CONT
2 CONT anledning till mycket prat. Hon var dotter till en af de rikaste krämare i Stockholm, den så
2 CONT
2 CONT kallade Pehr i Porten, emedan han hade sin handelsbod i det långa hvalf, som från nuvarande Benikebrinken i Stockholm gick ned till östra stadsporten, eller från Östra Långgatan och ner till sjön.
2 CONT
2 CONT – Agda fängslade Erik XIV, då kronprins, och förde med honom en så förtrolig sammanlefnad, att hon skänkte honom trenne döttrar, Lucretia, som dog helt späd, samt Virginia och Constantia, hvilka af deras höge fader erkändes, uppto
2 CONC gos till hofvet, sedan han blef konung, uppfostrades der, såsom prinsessor, och blefvo gifta med 
2 CONT
2 CONT ganska ansedde män. – Det var dock i Eriks aldraförsta ungdom, som han älskade Agda Pehrsdotter, och innan han lärde känna den oförlikneliga Catharina, den han sedan var obrottsligt trogen.
2 CONT
2 CONT – Agda blef, emot konungens vilja, besynnerligt nog, oaktadt sitt så mycket fläckade namn, sedermera gift (1561) med konung Erik XIV:s kammarjunkare Joachim Fleming. I detta gifte hade hon en dotter, Anna, som blef gift med hertig
2 CONC  Carls kammarjunkare Hieronymus von Birchholtz
2 CONT
2 CONT Källa: Anteckningar om Svenska kvinnor, Ståhlberg, 1864
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Called Agda "Charitas" for her beauty. Was the former mistress of King Erik XIV of Sweden.
2 CONT
2 CONT ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Wikipedia:
2 CONT
2 CONT "Agda Persdotter or Agda i Porten, (fl. 1565), was a Swedish woman, main royal mistress of King Eric XIV of Sweden during his time as a Crown Prince and during the first years of his reign 1560-1565.
2 CONT
2 CONT Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT Agda Persdotter is believed to have been the daughter of the wealthy merchant Peder Klementsson, who lived by St Nicolai port in Stockholm and was known as Pher i Porten, though her parentage has not been confirmed. She was descri
2 CONC bed as a great beauty, and was called Charitas. She became the mistress of Eric during his time as a crown prince, and is the first of his recorded mistresses. She was a center of his court at Kalmar Castle 1558, where a chamber, 
2 CONC Agdas kammare, (= "The Chamber of Agda") is still named after her. Their relationship continued after he became king in 1560.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1561, she was married to the noble Joakim Fleming and given the estate Eknaholm outside Växjö, which had belonged to a monastery. The relationship with Eric ended, and continued only after she became a widow in 1563. The relati
2 CONC onship was not exclusive, as Eric had a large number of other mistresses; during the period 1561-65, Anna Larsdotter, Karin Jacobsdotter, Karin Pedersdotter, Sigrid Nilsdotter, Doredi Valentinsdotter and the more anonymous Britta 
2 CONC and Ingrid was all listed as the King's mistresses, but Agda was his main mistress. The position of these women was only half official.
2 CONT
2 CONT She had several daughters with Eric, and one daughter with Joakim; Anna, (born 1562). In 1561, the custody of her children was given to the king's sister, Princess Cecilia of Sweden, because, as Eric said: "I know she is not capab
2 CONC le of raising them in good discipline and other things". When Cecilia left the country in 1564, the care, as well as the care of the other children of Eric, was given to Princess Elizabeth of Sweden. One of Elizabeth's servants, K
2 CONC arin Månsdotter, took care of Virginia. In 1565, Karin became the one and only mistress of Eric and replaced both Agda and all the others. Agda remarried the noble Christoffer Olsson Stråle av Sjöared, sheriff of Stegeborg.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Margareta Eriksdotter (1558–1618), married 1592 to Olov Simonsson, vicar of Horn.
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Virginia Eriksdotter (1559–1633) (living descendants)
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Constantia Eriksdotter (1560–1649) (living descendants)
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Lucretia Eriksdotter (1564–after 1574) died young.
2 CONT
2 CONT References
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Hans Gillingstam, "Agda Persdotter, hennes släkt och Erik XIV:s dotter Lucretia. En källkritisk studie", Släkt och Hävd 2001:2-3, s. 156-160.
2 CONT
2 CONT     * http://runeberg.org/sqvinnor/0012.html
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Herman Lindqvist, "Historien om Sverige: Gustav Vasa och hans söner och döttrar."
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Lars-Olof Larsson, "Arvet efter Gustav Vasa" "to be found at: - http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Agda_Persdotter
2 CONT
2 CONT * Agda Persdotter är bara mor åt Constantia inte till Sigrid de är halvsystrar.
2 CONT
2 CONT * Hans Gillingstam, "Agda Persdotter, hennes släkt och Erik XIV:s dotter Lucretia. En källkritisk studie", Släkt och Hävd 2001:2-3, s. 156-160.
2 CONT * Gadd, Pia: Frillor, fruar och herrar - en okänd kvinnohistoria Falun 2009
2 CONT
2 CONT * http://sv.wikipedia.org/wiki/Agda_Persdotter, Agda Persdotter
2 CONT
2 CONT * Agda Persdotter ("Agda i porten"), med okända födelse- och dödsår, var Erik XIV:s frilla under Kalmartiden. Hon har uppgivits vara dotter till rådmannen Peder Klemetsson i S:t Nicolai port (i Stockholm), en uppgift som dock hitt
2 CONC ills har varit omöjlig att verifiera. Agda kallades "Charitas" för sin skönhets skull. Hon ersattes som kungens favorit 1564-65 (då hade hon varit gift sedan år 1561) av Karin Månsdotter. Agda gifte sig 1561 med kammarjunkaren Joa
2 CONC chim Fleming (troligen död 1563). Med honom hade hon en dotter Anna (född 1562)
2 CONT
2 CONT Agda Persdotter hade åtminstone två döttrar med kungen, Virginia och Constantia:
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Virginia Eriksdotter (1559-1633), gift med landshövdingen Håkan Knutsson (Hand).
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Constantia Eriksdotter (1560-1649), gift med häradshövdingen Henrik Frankelin (död 1610), känd för sina långa resor i östra Europa.
2 CONT
2 CONT En tredje utomäktenskaplig dotter till Erik XIV, Lucretia (född 1564), har förmodats vara dotter till Agda, men det finns inga belägg för detta. Hon uppges i en källa ha varit gift med en Daniel Zelow.
2 CONT
2 CONT Litteratur [redigera]
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Hans Gillingstam, "Agda Persdotter, hennes släkt och Erik XIV:s dotter Lucretia. En källkritisk studie", Släkt och Hävd 2001:2-3, s. 156-160.
2 CONT
