1 OCCU Riddare, riksråd (troligen mellan åren 1319-1328).
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Torkel Andersson (båt)=
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT *  Christine “ Kristina” Ulfsdotter (Ama). Was married to the knight and the national council Torkel Andersson (split shield, later boat), who calls Holmger Ulfsson dy his "genes" 1311, seals brother Lars Ulfsson's first will 1313
2 CONC  and Ulf Holmgersson d. Y's will 1335 and must have had a son named Holmger Torkelsson (Båat), named after one of his early deceased uncles.
2 CONT * Torkel was married to a sister of Holmger; see ÄSF I, p. 108.
2 CONT * A branch of the family dropped the name Svinhufvud as early as the 17th century, and called itself Qvist.
2 CONT
2 CONT =The Swedish Diplomatarium's National Archives  of Medieval Letters=
2 CONT
2 CONT == SDHK No:[https://sok.riksarkivet.se/?Sokord=Torkel+Andersson&EndastDigitaliserat=false&AvanceradSok=False&page=1&postid=sdhk_2405&tab=post&FacettState=undefined%3Ac%7C#tab 2405]
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Dating: 1311 March 12, of Issue: Stockholm'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Torkel Andersson announces that he and his brother-in-law Holmger Ulfsson (dy) exchanged property in such a way that he hands over to him and his heirs 2 farms in Torpa, 2 farms in Mellby (Mälby in Torshälla parish) and 2 mills in
2 CONC  Torshälla while Holmger gave the issuer and his heirs their estates in Länna (?; "Lennom") and Kalvstad. Witnesses and sailors are Mr. Mattias Kettilmundsson, Mr. Sigmund Erengislesson, Mr. Torkel Djäkne, Lars Ulfsson and Nils Vä
2 CONC nundsson. - https://sok.riksarkivet.se/dokument/sdhk/2405.pdf
2 CONT
2 CONT == SDHK No: [https://sok.riksarkivet.se/?Sokord=Torkel+Andersson&EndastDigitaliserat=false&AvanceradSok=False&page=122&FacettState=undefined%3Ac%7C&postid=sdhk_4146&tab=post#tab 4146]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Swedish Diplomatarium's main directory of medieval letters'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Dating: 1335 April 5
2 CONT
2 CONT Ulf Holmgersson, canoe in Uppsala and Västerås, wills to Uppsala Cathedral's building, where he chooses to be buried, a farm in Helgestad, and to improve the prebend he held in Västerås 6 Öresland in Ulsa and 1 Öresland in Vikby. 
2 CONC He decides numerous gifts in the form of money and other things to. a. Strängnäs Cathedral, Linköping Cathedral, Vårfruberga Monastery, Kristina Holmgersdotter, Alvastra Monastery, Nydala Monastery, Varnhem Monastery, Julita Monas
2 CONC tery, Preachers Brothers in Strängnäs, Sigtuna, Västerås, Skara, Lödöse, Frännaö, Skänninge, Kalänninge Söderköping, Linköping, Jönköping, Skara, Arboga, Enköping, on to Sko monastery, Askeby monastery, S: take Klara monastery in 
2 CONC Stockholm, the whole house in Uppsala, the leprosy house in Enköping, the hospital in Strängnäs, Söderköping, Skänninge,
2 CONT
2 CONT King Magnus, Torkel Andersson, Birger Magnusson, and the issuer seal, SEAL
2 CONT The seal: N: o 1-5 away, the strips left; N: o 6, Ulf Holmgerssons (3 plugs). - https://www.geni.com/photo/view?album_type=photos_of_me&id=6000000049027095883&photo_id=6000000140042367915&position=0
2 CONT
2 CONT == SDHK-nr: [https://sok.riksarkivet.se/?Sokord=Torkel+Andersson&EndastDigitaliserat=false&AvanceradSok=False&page=116&FacettState=undefined%3Ac%7C&postid=sdhk_3068&tab=post#tab 3068]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Swedish Diplomatarium's main directory of medieval letters'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Dating: 1321  januari  27, Issue: Varberg
2 CONT
2 CONT King Magnus renews and affirms the Duchesses of Ingeborg's and Ingeborg's measure to restore Lena's farm in Västergötland to Linköping's cathedral.
2 CONT
2 CONT The issuer and the duchesses Ingeborg and Ingeborg, Archbishop Olof in Uppsala, Mathias Kettilmundsson, Knut Jonsson, Birger Petersson, Knut Magnusson, Ture Kettilsson, Bo Nilsson, Håkan Jonsson Læma, Lars Ulfsson, Torkel Andersso
2 CONC n, Sune Jonsson and Knut Porse. - https://www.geni.com/photo/view/6000000007328999766?album_type=photos_of_me&photo_id=6000000140043104006
2 CONT
2 CONT == SDHK No: [https://sok.riksarkivet.se/?Sokord=Torkel+Andersson&EndastDigitaliserat=false&AvanceradSok=False&page=118&FacettState=undefined%3Ac%7C&postid=sdhk_3277&tab=post#tab 3277]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Swedish Diplomatarium's main directory of medieval letters'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Dating: 1324 April 11, of Issue: Kalmar'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Duke Valdemar's widow Ingeborg documents Archbishop Olofs in Uppsala, Birger Perssons, Knut Jonssons, Tore Kettilssons, Bo Nilssons, Torkel Anderssons, Stefan Rörikssons and Tord Bonde's certificate in Stockholm in 1320, concernin
2 CONC g the settlement that was entered into between the clan and prior entry Håkan Läma regarding her donation of certain goods to the abbey.
2 CONT
2 CONT The issuer and Håkan Ingeborgsson seal. - https://www.geni.com/photo/view/6000000007328999766?album_type=photos_of_me&photo_id=6000000140042556498
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://sok.riksarkivet.se/sbl/Presentation.aspx?id=13177 Branch, Family]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''By the Swedish Biographical Dictionary'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Gren, medieval family of salvation, whose family name can be traced back to 1424 at the earliest. of the years 1312—19. The former son Inge Kettilbjörnsson (still living in 1335) became a knight shortly before his death. His broth
2 CONC er Ernils Kettilbjörnsson (still living in 1330), known as one of those who in 1320 for King Magnus Eriksson's guardian government negotiated with King Birger's followers in Viborg, became the father of Harald Ernilsson (still ali
2 CONC ve in 1360). He probably married a dtr descended from his mother from Earl Birger to the councilor Torkel Andersson (boat).
2 CONT
2 CONT In the 1370s, their son Torkel Haraldsson (d. 1402) had to make pilgrimages to Rome, Aachen and Nidaros for a murder. Later he was district chief in several districts in Södermanland and Östergötland. Torkel Haraldsson was dubbed 
2 CONC a knight in the autumn of 1389, probably at the Lord's Day in Söderköping, where Queen Margaret took power in Sweden, and was later named courtier at Ämnisholm in Småland. In 1398 he was a member of King Erik's Union Council, but 
2 CONC he never belonged to the Swedish National Council.
2 CONT
2 CONT His brother, the district chief in Österrekarne (Söd) Sten Haraldsson (still living 1417) on Ål (now Grensholmen) in Vånga (Ög), married a daughter of King Erik Magnusson's councilor Nils Magnusson (Ivar Nilsson's family) father o
2 CONC f Riksrådet Magnus G (G 1). His son Councilor Ivar G (G 2) became the father of Councilor Måns G (G 3). Family G died out with two of the latter's sisters, who were still alive in the early 1540s. Among its descendants on the wome
2 CONC n's side was King Gustav I, whose grandmother's mother was the niece of G 1. The family 
2 CONT
2 CONT name survives in the farm name Grensholmen. Namely, G l's manor was called Ål from around 1510 by his son-in-law Erik Ryning, who then owned it.
2 CONT
