1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Magnus Nilsson=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Married:  Ingrid Rodsdotter 
2 CONT * Birth:	before 1290
2 CONT * Death:	after September 19, 1329
2 CONT
2 CONT =Children=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Nils Magnusson
2 CONT * Abjorn Magnusson 
2 CONT * Arvid Magnusson
2 CONT * Cecilia Magnusdotter
2 CONT
2 CONT =History=
2 CONT
2 CONT Ivar Nilsson's family is a conventional term for a Swedish medieval high-salvation family who, like Lindöätten, had a four-piece shield as his seal weapon. As the ancestor of the family, one is counted only through the son's patro
2 CONC nymic known man Nils, who should have been born in the second half of the 13th century.
2 CONT
2 CONT The son Magnus Nilsson was a national council and is mentioned living 1305-1329. His seat yard was Villberga in the parish with the same name in Trögden, Uppland. The name Ivar entered the family first in the third known generatio
2 CONC n, when Nils grandson Nils Magnusson married a daughter to the feathers in Tønsberg, which was called Ivar Nilsson. Nils Magnusson is mentioned in 1356 as King Erik's advice.
2 CONT
2 CONT The family died out in the early 15th century.
2 CONT
2 CONT =Sources=
2 CONT
