1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Hinse Jönsson Svinhufvud=
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT * Son of Jöns Hansson Svinhufvud and Ragnhild NN 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://sok.riksarkivet.se/sbl/Mobil/Artikel/34993#/sbl/Mobil/Artikel/10305 Knut Andersson (Lillie), by Swedish Biographical Dictionary]
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Knut Andersson, d 1546 between 29 April and 19 December. Parents: gunsmith Anders Laurensson (Lillie) and a daughter (Barbro?) to Hinse Jönsson (Svinhuvud; see Gillingstam 1968-69). Earliest mentioned 16, one of the two chief offi
2 CONC cers for Gustav Eriksson's (Vasa) warriors at Rotebro north of Sthlm autumn 21, riksråd 2 (Bärätelse ... 1523) or 3 (GIR) June 23, lawman in Södermanland 15 Jan 26, knight at King Gustav's coronation 12 Jan 28, one of the three Ri
2 CONC ksrårds at the head of the castle law on Sthlm 8 Nov 31, häradsh in Frötuna and Länna ship teams probably at the latest 36, also in Sjuhundra hd and Bro o Vätö ships team 5 Feb 38, led by the regimental council at the latest 40.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://sok.riksarkivet.se/sbl/Presentation.aspx?id=34993&forceOrdinarySite=true Svinhufvud,  Volume 35 (2020-), page 23, by Swedish Biographical Lexicon]
2 CONT
2 CONT The above-mentioned Hinse Jönsson was the brother of the vicar Daniel Swinshowet (d trol 1503) in Mora, as can be seen from an inheritance dispute in 1492 when Daniel was agent for Hinse's children. Daniel has been identified with
2 CONC  the canon with the same first name who was buried in Västerås cathedral under a stone with a boar's head coat of arms and the year 1503 together with his mother Ragnhild in Höjen and his brother master Timme Swinshouet(Gardell; B
2 CONC erglund et al. 2008). Daniel and Timme had been enrolled at the University of Rostock in 1465 and 1466 respectively as "Daniel Swineshouet de Arusia" (Västerås) and "Tymo Swinshouet de Arosia" and continued their studies in 1467 i
2 CONC n Greifswald, where Timme became a bachelor in 1468. That they had the same patronymic as Hinse Jönsson is evident in the case of Daniel from a parchment letter from 1471 and in the case of Timme from the register of the Universit
2 CONC y of Cologne, where he was enrolled in 1477 and became a master in 1478. In 1487 the Pope granted the latter's request for the position of deacon in Västerås, which he had to leave as early as 1489. Daniel according to a papal dis
2 CONC pensation from 1465, in his youth had been in military service with King Karl Knutsson (Bonde) and later participated in Archbishop Jöns Bengtsson's (Oxenstierna; vol. 28)rebellion against the same king (Winroth 2011). He is menti
2 CONC oned in 1467 and 1471 as a canon in Västerås, and received the aforementioned vicarage in Mora in 1484 and was a priest at Kopparberget in 1500.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT =Sources=
