1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * http://personen.digitale-sammlungen.de/baltlex/Blatt_bsb00000602,00025.html?prozent=* 
2 CONT * http://www.adelsvapen.com/genealogi/Bagge_af_Boo_nr_122
2 CONT * http://vesture.eu/index.php?title=Att%C4%93ls:Baron_Bagge_af_Boo_Wappen.png&limit=100
2 CONT * https://sv.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jakob_Bagge
2 CONT
2 CONT ______________________________________________________________________
2 CONT
2 CONT ** http://sv.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jakob_Bagge
2 CONT
2 CONT *** http://fi.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jakob_Bagge
2 CONT
2 CONT **** http://runeberg.org/minnespfin/2/0026.html
2 CONT
2 CONT Jakob (James?) Tordsson Bagge, born 1502 , died 1577 , Swedish admiral and governor . 
2 CONT
2 CONT Biography 
2 CONT
2 CONT James Bagge was born in May 1502 of Halland or Norway as the son of Thord Olofsson Bagge and Ingeborg Jacob's daughter, both of Norwegian noble birth. Both he and his father was the first in the Danish service, but entered the Swe
2 CONC dish service for Gustav Vasa 1522nd Bagge was first known as the sheriff, but was already in 1534 captain of a fänika soldiers and participated in the Count feud as a commander on both land and sea. 1535 he defeated John of Hoya i
2 CONC n Halmstad. 1541 he became the admiral in the navy. During Dacke rising , he became war chief and played a major role in the crackdown Smalanders after Nils Dacke's death. 
2 CONT
2 CONT During the war with Russia in the 1550s participated Bagge as field colonel and received the nobility by King Gustav Vasa, who also gave him great fiefs. His most brilliant feats performed Jacob Bagge during the Northern Seven Yea
2 CONC rs 1563-70 when he took command of the Swedish Navy, and he attended May 30, 1563 in the battle against the Danish island of Bornholm, which was cause for the outbreak of war. In the famous battle he defeated the Danish fleet, and
2 CONC  took its admiral Joakim Brock houses to catch, why King Eric had the victor holding a shining triumph in Stockholm. He was seen as a great war hero. At first the battle at northern tip of Öland in May 1564, his flagship in March 
2 CONC also called Jutehataren or Makalös rudder shot away. The Danes went into it and took the Beetle to capture. He was taken to Copenhagen, where he was held for seven years. 
2 CONT
2 CONT On his return to Stockholm, he was appointed in 1571 to the castle holidays (commander) at the Royal Palace and died there January 14, 1577. He was also lord of Boo yard and Mem castle . His wife was Anna Svinhufvud, with whom he 
2 CONC had two sons, Jacob Jr. and John. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Trivia Both Baggensfjärden , Baggensstäket , Baggensgatan and torpedo cruiser HMS Jacob Bagge has been named after him. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Literature
2 CONT
2 CONT Lars-Ove Larsson , Who's Who in Swedish history
2 CONT
2 CONT Swedish encyclopedia , Lund 1929 
2 CONT
2 CONT Swedish biographical own lexicon 
2 CONT
2 CONT Nordic family lexicon
2 CONT
2 CONT * http://www.nad.riksarkivet.se/sbl/Presentation.aspx?id=18993
