1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Gudmund Torbjörnsson Gumsehuvud=
2 CONT
2 CONT Häradshövdingen i Väne härad Torbjörn Esgersson, tydligen son av Esger, upptog morfaderns vapen, bagghuvudet, vilket han förde 1459 och sedermera, liksom dennes son Gudmund  Torbjörnsson, häradshövding efter fadern 1486–1495, med 
2 CONC vars dotter Forstena övergick till den yngre Forstena-
2 CONT släkten. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Ägde gården Forstena i Älvsborg som övertogs av dottern Anna vid giftet med Torsten Brunsson Sparre. 
2 CONT
2 CONT * To the Forstena, of the older Forstena family. Wore a bagghuvud in the weapon. District Judge in Väne HD after the Father 1486-1495. Source: Elgenstierna 
2 CONT * Gudmund Bjurum (Torbjörn's son)
2 CONT * District Judge in Väne, County 1486-1495. 
2 CONT * Father: Torbjörn Bjurum (son of Eskil) children
2 CONT * To Forstena, of the older Forstena family. Carried a beetle head in the weapon. District chief in Väne hd after the father 1486-1495.  Source: Elgenstierna
2 CONT
2 CONT =Married=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Married:''' Ragnhild Svensdotter (half lily),''' daughter of Väpnare Sven Johansson Halv lilja and Ingeborg Toresdotter Byting, till Stola 
2 CONT
2 CONT =Children=
2 CONT
2 CONT *''' Anna Bjurum (Gudmundsdotter);''' Anna Gudmundsdotter, daughter of Häradshövdingen in Väne hundred Gudmund torbjörns Son (Bagghuvud), to Forstena, of the elder Forstenasläkten, and Ragnhild svensdotter (half lily).
2 CONT * '''Gudmund Gudmundsson (Gumsehuvud,)''' Source: Theutenberg, between the lily and the lake leaf, p 447
2 CONT
2 CONT ='''Swedish Diplomatarium's Main Directory of Medieval Letters'''=
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://sok.riksarkivet.se/?Sokord=Gudmund+Torbj%C3%B6rnsson+&EndastDigitaliserat=false&Fritext=Gudmund+Torbj%C3%B6rnsson+&AvanceradSok=True&page=1&postid=sdhk_33241&tab=post&FacettState=undefined%3Ac%7C#tab SDHK No: 33241]
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://www.geni.com/photo/view/6000000006829132251?album_type=photos_of_me&photo_id=6000000131147228844 Orginal Document, Original:  Or. Perg. RA 0101  pictures]
2 CONT Post-medieval regest / note:  Misc. 71: 9 (reg.) 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Dating: 1495 June 3, of issue, here City''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT Issuer Gudmund Torbjörnsson in Forstene, gunner and chief of the county in Väne,
2 CONT
2 CONT Gudmund Torbjörnsson in Forstena, gunner and governor in Väne hardened, and others certify that Olof Asmundsson and Gunne Asmundsson in "Hwidenæ" managed and handled his grandfather Orm Jensson on Nils Klaussons, the chief's man i
2 CONC n Älvsborg, on behalf of a mill in Åsad .
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://www.adelsvapen.com/genealogi/Forstenasl%C3%A4kten_nr_2 Adliga Forstenas gengen # 2]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Ancient family of salvation, introduced in 1625.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT The genus, which at the mother originated from the family of the Abjörnsons (see the noble family Bagge af Berga). received at the introduction the name Forstenas Family after its then main farm Forstena in Tunhem's parish, in Vän
2 CONC e herded Älvsborgs county, which, however, was acquired rather late. This farm was formerly owned by a family that initially carried a lake leaf in the weapon, which was subsequently changed to a rear head. Of this older Forstena 
2 CONC family, the following are known. The brothers Åke and Esger Torbjörnssons appear during the years 1415–1435, the latter married 1418 at Forstena to Ingrid Siggesdotter, daughter of the gunman Sigge Birgersson, who is named in the 
2 CONC documents 1405–1417 and in the arms carried a rear head, and apparently owned Forstena (he was 1413 resides in Väne hierad). Both of these brothers carried an unsheathed sea leaf or heart in the weapon. The governor of Väne cured 
2 CONC Torbjörn Esgersson, apparently the son of Esger, took up his grandfather's weapon, the rear head, which he led in 1459 and later, as did his son Gudmund Torbjörnsson, governor after the father 1486–1495, with whose daughter Forste
2 CONC na passed to the younger Forstena family. Whether there was a relationship between these and Sven Brynjulfsson, who carried the rear head, is unknown. The family has branched out into the gracious family Torstenson, no. 7. Another
2 CONC  branch of the family has been introduced specifically with the name Ultfana.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Source''' Adel Weapon Wiki 
2 CONT
