1 NAME Botvid /Larsson/ d.ä.
2 GIVN Botvid
2 NSFX d.ä.
2 _MARNM Larsson
2 NICK Skrivare
2 NICK till Agnhammer
2 NICK the elder
1 SEX M
1 DEAT
2 DATE 31 DEC 1550
2 ADDR
3 CITY Bro (C)
3 CTRY Sweden
1 BURI
2 DATE 2 JAN 1551
2 PLAC Gråbrödaklostret
2 ADDR
3 CITY Stockholm
3 CTRY Sweden
1 OCCU Lagman i Värmland
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.adelsvapen.com/genealogi/Anckar_nr_108
2 CONT
2 CONT aka Bothvid Larsson the elder of Agnhammer and Aspeberg; aka Bothvid Skrivare, son of Lars (Lasse) Bothvidsson the elder of Agnhammar, Grums parish, Värmland. He Died on his estate in Bro, buried January 2nd, 1551 in what was form
2 CONC erly known as Gråbrödraklostret, the monastery whose church is now called Riddarholmskyrkan. He became Sheriff over Värmland in 1530, Judge in 1538, and he established Värmlands first land register "Jordeboken 1540 för Värmland". 
2 CONC He became Bailiff at Stockholms Royal Palace in 1541. In 1542 during the peasant uprising in Småland known as the Dacke fued, he was a military commander who defended King Gustav Vasa's cause. He was Sheriff over Stockholm's Royal
2 CONC  Palace and city from 1543 until his death. In 1541 he received Älvdals County in fief, Fryksdalen district in 1543, and Nordmark District May 16, 1546. In 1544 he was a member of the nobility in Vesterås. He married Karin Kart, w
2 CONC ho lived as his widow at Agnhammar, Grums, Värmland in 1565, she was the daughter of Sven Kart of Nygard and Åmor and his wife Kjerstin Thorsteinsdottor in Wånga. Bothvid Larsson's widow inherited the estate of her brother Peder K
2 CONC art who was ennobled by King Gustav Vasa on May 7 1556 and given a coat of arms with an anchor upon the shield. The descendants of Bothvid Larsson and Karin Kart began using the family crest and adopted the surname Anckar, Ancher,
2 CONC  and Anker which survives today in Sweden, Norway, and beyond.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Ramsay, Jully: Frälsesläkter i Finland intill stora ofreden. s. 240;
2 CONT
2 CONT Botvid Larsson till Agnhammar.  (Son af Lars Botvidsson, till Agnhammar i Grums  socken, Värmland) Befallningsman i Värmland 1530. Underlagman 1538. Befallningsman på Stockholms slott 1543; † 1550, begrafven i Gråbrödraklostret i 
2 CONC Stockholm. Gift med Karin Kart.  Barn: se  Anrep: Anckar, tab. I. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Anrep, Gabriel;  Svenska adelns ättar-taflor.  s. 52:
2 CONT
2 CONT Bothwld Larsson, den Äldre, annars Bothwid Skrifvare kallad, till Agn hammar; Befallningsman öfver Wermland 1530; Under-Lagman derst. 1538; Fogde på Stockholms slott 1541 ; Knekte-Höfvidsman emot Nils Dacke 1542; Befallningsman på
2 CONC  Stockholms slott och stad 1543;  †  31.12.1550 på sin gård i Bro socken och begrafven i Gråbrödraklostret i Stockholm.  Gift med Carin Kart, som lefde enka på Agnhammar 1565; dotter af Befallningsmannen öfver Wermland, sedermera 
2 CONC Slottslofven på Leckö, Sven Kart till Anior och Nygård med Kjerstin Thorstensdotter i Wånga. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Agnhammar
2 CONT
2 CONT https://sbvfvarmland.wordpress.com/2009/09/30/nu-skrivs-slutkapitlet-i-historien-om-agnhammars-herrgard/
2 CONT
2 CONT Dess historia från 1547 till 1646 är intimt förbunden med ätten Anckar, vars män spelat stor roll i Värmlands historia under Vasatiden Den mest berömda var Botvid Larsson Anckar, fogde över Värmland 1530-1546 och mannen bakom den 
2 CONC äldsta jordboken, ett dokument som inget land äger motstycke till. 
2 CONT
2 CONT -----
