2 CONC e gone to Germany and settled there in the midst of a raging war, and there is no proof because he would have been transported to another regiment after the muster in 1644, one should probably take for granted the knight's house g
2 CONC enealogy's statement that he "died in Skåne". As far as we know, no proof of the relationship between the Stårck family and the German von Storck family has been provided. The last mentioned family, which at the elevation to royal
