1 NAME Cecilia /Hansdotter Svinhufvud/
2 GIVN Cecilia
2 SURN Hansdotter Svinhufvud
2 _MARNM Hansdotter Svinhufvud
1 SEX F
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Cecilia Hansdotter=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Daughter of Hans Jönsson Svinhufvud and Ingeborg Larsdotter
2 CONT * https://www.geni.com/photo/view?album_type=photos_of_me&id=6000000002527990452&photo_id=6000000085118361979&position=1
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://sok.riksarkivet.se/sbl/Presentation.aspx?id=34993&forceOrdinarySite=true Svinhufvud Family, by The Swedish Biographical Lexicon]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Volume 35 (2020-), page 23.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT The genealogical information about a Qvist family branch is found in the appendix to an application for nobility in 1785 by Bengt Qvist Andersson (bd 29) , whose information proved to be unverifiable upon investigation. 
2 CONT The boar's head coat of arms was also carried by the aforementioned miner Jöns Hansson's sister Cecilia's son Nils Månsson in her marriage to Magnus Henriksson Svart, who was killed at the latest in 1468 (Winroth 2001). Nils Månss
2 CONC on (d sometime between 1500–04) in Aspeboda, Aspeboda parish, was a judge, mountain master and mountain bailiff at Kopparberget and father of the previously mentioned mountain bailiff and district chief Måns Nilsson, who was execu
2 CONC ted in 1534 after the bell rebellion. Måns Nilsson's daughter Anna Månsdotter (d at the earliest in 1595) was married to the mountain man Hans Persson(d some of the years 1564–68) in Surarvet, Aspeboda parish, a brother of the afo
2 CONC rementioned district magistrate Jöns Persson in Risholn (E8676). Their son Albrekt Hansson (d 1631) in Aspeboda took over the pig's head coat of arms from his grandfather. He served from 1591–1623 as district judge and then distri
2 CONC ct chief in Dalarna and was a member of the estate court at the Linköping massacre in 1600 (Berglund o Winroth 2010).
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT =History=
2 CONT
2 CONT The origins of the egg can be brought back on a parchment letter from 1386 when a Jöns Swinshwow bought the two farms Höjen and Stenbjörnsarvet (now Stämnarvet) in Torsångs parish (now Stora Kopparbergs parish). The text is partly
2 CONC  altered, possibly in connection with the letter being shown up in the autumn tea in Sundborn in 1673 by, among others, the mountain man Olof Nilsson at Höjen. However, surveys of the document indicate that from the very beginning
2 CONC , there was a pig head.
2 CONT
2 CONT The mountaineer at Kopparberget, Hans Jönsson (mentioned 1434–1439), as well as his brother Dan Jönsson, the vicar of Hedemora parish 1405–1427, brought a pig's head in his weapon.
2 CONT
2 CONT Hans Jönsson was the father of Jöns Hansson, a mountain master at Kopparberget 1450 and, according to a later assignment from Rasmus Ludvigsson, will have lived on the hill. Another son was Jeppe Hansson, who signed up for Risholn
2 CONC  (then in Svärdsjö, later Sundborn's parish). From his son Hans Jeppesson in Risholn (dead before 1540) and his daughter, Svinhufvud in Westergötland leads his ancestry.
2 CONT
2 CONT Hans Jönsson's second daughter Cecilia was married to Magnus Henriksson Svart. Their son mountain bailiff at Kopparberget Nils Månsson, in turn, became the father of Måns Nilsson (Svinhufvud). From his daughter-in-law Per Hanson, 
2 CONC the noble family of Svinhufvud stems from Qvalstad. Per Hansson's brother the ruler Albrekt Hansson (dead 1631) in Aspeboda has left a lot of descendants in Dalarna and neighboring landscapes.
2 CONT
2 CONT Gudlög Hansdotter, daughter of Hans Jönsson (mentioned 1434–1439), through his marriage with Jeppe Henriksson (Simla) in Karlborn, Svärdsjö parish, was requesting noble and Countess Ekeblad.
2 CONT
2 CONT The rock scribe Hans Jönsson was the father of the priests Daniel and Timme Jönsson, who when they were enrolled at Rostock University in 1465 and 1466 were the first to use the surname Svinhufvud as a surname. Their sister-in-law
2 CONC , Västeråsbiskopen Otto Svinhufvud, also took up the name when he was enrolled in 1480 at Rostock University.
2 CONT
