1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Ingel Hansson=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Son of Hans Jeppesson Svinhufvud and Margareta Ulfsdotter
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/photo/view?album_type=photos_of_me&id=4729151&photo_id=6000000194351758823&position=0 '''Vem var dalafogden Ingel Hanssons (Svinhuvud) hustru pà Gylle? Av Stefan Jernberg'.''']
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/photo/view/4729151?album_type=photos_of_me&photo_id=6000000194354362822 The sheriff and magistrate Ingel Gregersson in St Tuna descended on the paternal line from the Svinhuvud family - his grandfather was 
2 CONC the executed bailiff Ingel Hansson in Gylle. However, the former does not seem to have used the Svinhuvudvapnet - at least not in 1615 (Älvsborg's ransom 1613, Commissioners' and others' accounts for the local collection of Älvsbo
2 CONC rg's ransom, SE/RA/5117/IV/45B (1615), image date: A0066050_00226 ).]
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://sok.riksarkivet.se/sbl/Presentation.aspx?id=34993&forceOrdinarySite=true Svinhufvud Family, by The Swedish Biographical Lexicon]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Volume 35 (2020-), page 23.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Hans Jeppesson's son Ingel Hansson (d 1534) in Gylle in Stora Tuna parish was a bailiff in Dalarna in 1527–28 and 1531 but was executed after the bell rebellion together with his cousin Måns Nilsson (bd 26) . '''His son Nils Ingel
2 CONC sson (d earliest 1600), who has been confused with a Finnish bailiff Nils Ingesson (Lokalf), was mayor of Västerås 1575–95. A grandson's son of this was introduced in 1642 at Riddarhuset with the name Ikornsköld. Whether the famil
2 CONC y's unexpected coat of arms, a red squirrel on a blue field, is a misinterpretation of the boar's head coat of arms or is an adoption of the maternal coat of arms is uncertain. The family died out already in 1644.
2 CONT '''
2 CONT Ingel Hansson's half-sister Margareta Hansdotter was married to Jöns Persson (d at the earliest in 1564) at Risholn, who was district magistrate in Dalarna 1544–64 and received shield letter in 1561 (Samuelson), mother of Anna Jön
2 CONC sdotter . The latter's husband, the miner Daniel Torkelsson in Främby in Stora Kopparbergs parish, received a letter of shield in 1581 (Samuelson). Their son, the vicar Daniel Danielis Montanus (d 1588) in Vika used the boar's hea
2 CONC d coat of arms in his seal sometime between 1571 and 1577. His brother Jöns Danielsson(d 1613), who also bore the boar's head coat of arms, signed himself up to Främby and from 1583 was bailiff in various fiefdoms in Dalarna. Some
2 CONC  of his descendants came to live in Västergötland and Dalsland, which is why this family branch at Riddarhuset is called S in Westergötland . Numerous officers have belonged to it, seven of whom took part in Charles XII's war.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT =Sources=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Jöns Persson or Jöns S : AdRP 1 (2nd ed., 1904); Almquist, a a 1960, p. 68; Salvation, 1:2 (1931); local; Reg to AdRP 1–17
2 CONT * Margareta Hansdotter and Anna Jönsdotter : E 8676, f 314 v, RA; J Samuelson, Aristocrat or Ennobled Peasant? (1993), p. 318
2 CONT * Hans Jeppesson : Littered judgment books and court trade, vol 24, RA; H Gillingstam, Rasmus Ludvigsson's and his wife's family connections (SoH 1950); Siggesson, a a 1937; STb 4 (1931); Sweden's medieval personal names, 3 (1995–
2 CONC 2006), sp 85 o 92.
2 CONT * Ingel Hansson : GIR 3–5, 7 o 9 (1865–85); Gillingstam, a a 1950; M Hallenberg, The King, the bailiffs and the kingdom (2001), pp. 163 ff; KI Hildeman, The Clock Rebellion (HT 1946), p 3 fo 27; Kumlien, aa; LO Larsson, Gustav Vas
2 CONC a (2002); local; Peder Svart, Gustav Vasa's Chronicle (1964); E Samuelsson, Medeltid og fiftendratal (Stora Tuna, 1959), pp. 181 o 196; Siggesson, a a 1937; Sjödin, Handlingar till Nordens historia 1515–23, 1 (HH 39, 1967–69), p 3
2 CONC 6; In Svalenius, Gustav Vasa (1963).
2 CONT * Nils Ingelsson : RR Jan–June 1600, f 26, RA; Kopparberg County District Court Archives, AI:2, f 39, ULA. O Bergström, Icorn shield (SAT II, ​​1897); KA Bomansson, Hertig Johan och hans tid (1862), p 105; Gillingstam, a a 1950; K
2 CONC umlien, aa; J Liedgren, Erik XIV's guard at Västerås castle 1573–74 (Västmanland's antiquities association's yearbook, 42, 1960), p 22; local; AA v Stiernman, Svea and Götha höfdinga-minne, 1–2 (1835–36); F Ödberg, About the stamp
2 CONC s against King Johan III in the years 1572–75 (1897), pp. 93, 113, 210, 212 o 231 f
